{
  "raw": {
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001F9": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (260001F9)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (260001F9) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (260001F9) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) - ( 260001F9 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Physics Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/ are filled Post(s) Specification: The Department of Physics invites applications for tenure-track or tenured faculty positions (at all ranks) from the academic year 2026-27. Outstanding candidates working in the areas of physics and materials science currently being pursued in the Department, are welcome to apply, including: - Astrophysics and Cosmology; - Atomic, Molecular, and Optical Physics; - Biophysics and Soft Matter Physics; - Complex Systems and Fluids; - Condensed Matter Physics; - Materials Science; - Quantum Information Science and Technology; - Particle Physics; and - Quantum Information Science and Technology. Applicants should (i) have a relevant PhD degree with postdoctoral research experience; (ii) demonstrate a track record of research accomplishments, potential for establishing a significant externally funded research programme; and (iii) have a strong interest in teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment(s) or substantiation. Application Procedure Applicants should submit an online application and attach a full resume, research plan, teaching statement, copies of academic credentials, a publication list and/ or abstracts of selected published papers (if any), together with names, addresses and fax numbers/ e-mail addresses of three referees to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references (unless otherwise specified). Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post(s) above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Physics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600012C": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600012C)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600012C) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600012C) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 2600012C ) Description Department/Unit: School of Life Sciences Closing Date: October 31, 2026 Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in life sciences, biomedical sciences, or related disciplines; and (ii) demonstrated research ability and experience in cell biology, molecular biology, patient iPSC-derived neuron and animal models, biological drug studies (in vitro and in vivo), or other advanced omics analytical skills, such as transcriptomics. Applicants with at least four years of relevant postdoctoral experience and a strong publication record are preferred. Track records in securing competitive research grants and experience in neurological disease mechanistic studies and/or drug discovery research would be an advantage. The appointee is expected to (a) seek and secure external research grants; (b) conduct research in neurological disease mechanisms and/or drug discovery; (c) co-supervise postgraduate students; and (d) assist in laboratory management. The appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to satisfactory performance and mutual agreement. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload the following documents: (i) a full curriculum vitae; (ii) copies of academic credentials; (iii) a complete publication list; and (iv) the names and e-mail addresses of three to five referees (to whom the applicant’s consent has been given for providing references). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Life Sciences Unposting Date : Oct 31, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001FH": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001FH)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001FH) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001FH) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 260001FH ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Electronic Engineering Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Department of Electronic Engineering (EE) at the Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is seeking outstanding candidates for Research Assistant Professorship (RAP). RESEARCH AREA OF INTEREST Intelligent (Medical) Robotics, Image-Guided Procedures, VLA, WAM, Perception & Applications: Particularly, the main areas of interest include embodied AI-assisted procedures, Medical Image Processing, biorobotics & intelligent systems, multisensory perception, AI learning and control in image-guided procedures, medical mechatronics, continuum, and soft flexible robots and sensors, deployable motion generation, compliance modulation/sensing, cooperative and context-aware flexible/soft sensors/actuators in human environments. The appointee will have opportunities to work with an interdisciplinary team consisting of clinicians and researchers from robotics, AI & perception, imaging, and medicine. Applicants should have: (i) a Ph.D. degree in robotics, AI, Computer Science/Engineering, Electronic or Mechanical Engineering, medical physics, automation, or mechatronics background; (ii) preferably proven expertise in AI/robots/sensors, instrumentation, intelligent systems, magnetic actuation, ROS and general-purpose robotic control; (iii) fluency in written and spoken English; good organizational skills; the ability to work independently; a strong sense of responsibility; and self-motivation; (iv) outstanding academic records/publications or recognitions from worldwide top-ranking institutes; (v) postdoctoral experience or equivalent qualifications, which are typically expected; (vi) in-depth research and clear teaching statements; and (vii) successful records in securing research grants and teaching excellence, which are preferred though not compulsory. The appointee will work closely with Professor Hongliang Ren in the Department to enhance the existing strengths. The appointee is expected to: (a) be able to have top-tier research outputs and apply for RGC GRF grants and similar external competitive grants; (b) undertake some teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and (c) provide service at departmental, faculty and/or university levels. HOW TO APPLY To apply, please upload a full resume, copies of academic credentials, a publication list with soft copies of the five most representative publications, details of courses taught and evaluation results (if available), a research plan, a teaching statement, and the names and contact information of three to five referees. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance, funding availability and mutual agreement. Review of applications will begin as soon as possible and only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Applications will be accepted until the post is filled. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.ee.cuhk.edu.hk/ . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Electronic Engineering Unposting Date : Feb 20, 2027"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001FI": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001FI)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001FI) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001FI) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 260001FI ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Electronic Engineering Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Department of Electronic Engineering (EE) at the Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is seeking outstanding candidates for Research Assistant Professorship (RAP). RESEARCH AREA OF INTEREST The research focuses on developing advanced energy saving technologies that integrate innovative materials, devices, and systems to enable intelligent detection and optical modulation. Key areas include smart materials design, optical modulation, and machine learning design for applications in energy saving, encryption, anticounterfeiting and beyond. Applicants should have: (i) a PhD in Materials Sciences , Physics, Chemistry or a related discipline; (ii) a strong track record of research and publications in reputable journals, particularly in areas related to smart materials; (iii) excellent communication and interpersonal skills; and (iv) potential to become an independent researcher in obtaining future/sustained extramural funding and establishing significant externally-funded research programmes. The appointee will work closely with Professor Long Yi in the Department to enhance the existing strengths. The appointee is expected to: (a) be able to have top-tier research outputs and apply for RGC GRF grants and similar external competitive grants; (b) undertake some teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and (c) provide service at departmental, faculty and/or university levels. HOW TO APPLY To apply, please upload a full resume, copies of academic credentials, a publication list with soft copies of the five most representative publications, details of courses taught and evaluation results (if available), a research plan, a teaching statement, and the names and contact information of three to five referees. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance, funding availability and mutual agreement. Review of applications will begin as soon as possible and only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Applications will be accepted until the post is filled. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.ee.cuhk.edu.hk/ . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Electronic Engineering Unposting Date : Feb 20, 2027"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001EV": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (Fractional time) (260001EV) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (Fractional time) (260001EV) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant (Fractional time) - ( 260001EV ) Description Department/Unit: Faculty of Medicine and Department of Microbiology Closing Date: September 3, 2026 Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) a specialist qualification in Clinical Microbiology; (iii) at least 5 years of post-specialist qualification experience; (iv) substantial experience in teaching medical students; and (v) demonstrated leadership in medical education. The appointee will undertake and coordinate undergraduate and postgraduate teaching activities, support curriculum development, and contribute to the advancement of medical education. In addition to fulfilling clinical teaching duties, he/she should demonstrate a strong commitment to educational excellence and innovation. Appointment will be made on a contract basis for an initial term of up to three years, renewable subject to satisfactory performance and mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Medicine Unposting Date : Sep 3, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001DJ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Clinical Lecturer (260001DJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Lecturer (260001DJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Lecturer (260001DJ) Job Description Clinical Lecturer - ( 260001DJ ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Orthopaedics and Traumatology Closing Date: Until the post is filled Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for full registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) experience/strong interest in orthopaedics and traumatology; and (iii) experience/strong interest in medical teaching. The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate courses; (b) provide medical service in orthopaedics and traumatology units; and (c) conduct clinical studies. The appointee will work at the Prince of Wales Hospital in Shatin. Appointment will initially be made on fixed-term contract basis for up to three years commencing Jan 2027 or as soon as possible, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Orthopaedics and Traumatology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001AO": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260001AO)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260001AO) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260001AO) Job Description Teaching Assistant - ( 260001AO ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Hotel and Tourism Management Closing date: Until the position is filled The School of Hotel and Tourism Management, CUHK Business School, is inviting applications for the position of Teaching Assistant for its MSc in Real Estate programme. Applicants should have: (i) a good Bachelor's degree; (ii) excellent communication skills in written and spoken English, as well as spoken Chinese (Cantonese and/or Mandarin); (iii) good people skill and proactive work attitude; (iv) the ability to assist in tutorials, laboratory/practical classes, compilation of course materials, and other academic activities under guidance; and (v) proficiency in Microsoft Office (e.g. Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and on-line teaching tactics. The appointee will support course teacher in daily pre-course planning, coordinate teaching and student related activities, perform teaching-related administrative tasks using various platforms (Blackboard, Veriguide, CATME, Kahoot etc). He/she will also work with other administrative staff in the department to support various school events and programme administrative duties. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for two years commencing October 2026, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Hotel and Tourism Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001AA": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (AI and Computational Communication) (260001AA)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (AI and Computational Communication) (260001AA) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (AI and Computational Communication) (260001AA) Job Description Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (AI and Computational Communication) - ( 260001AA ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Journalism and Communication Closing Date: Until the post is filled The School is seeking outstanding candidates, early career or established social scientists, with expertise in the area of AI and computational communication, to join the expanding faculty team as Professor / Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor. The faculty member is expected to contribute to the teaching of the School’s undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. The School welcomes candidates using qualitative, quantitative, or mixed-methods approaches, and a variety of theoretical orientations. Applicants should have (i) a PhD in Communication or other related fields; (ii) a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; and (iii) (for Professor/ Associate Professor) a proven record of research and publications in major journals; (for Assistant Professor) demonstrated potential/ ability for research and a cohesive research agenda. Applicants capable of engaging in interdisciplinary research and collaboration are preferred. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications will be offered. The comprehensive benefit package provided by the University includes generous academic leave, annual leave, medical care, retirement scheme contributions, contract-end gratuity, and housing benefits. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2027, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Outstanding candidates for Professor rank may be specially considered for substantive appointments forthwith. The School of Journalism and Communication has a strong focus on research and provides its members with solid support for their research work. Faculty members are productive and committed researchers as well as devoted educators. The faculty team at the School features a combination of highly promising young scholars and established scholars who are leaders in their own fields, including two elected Fellows of the International Communication Association. The School is ranked #16 globally in communication and media studies by the QS World University Ranking by Subject in 2026. The School has a strong tradition of upholding freedom of the press, of expression, and of academic research. To explore the School further, please visit our website at http://www.com.cuhk.edu.hk/ . Application Procedure To apply for the post, please complete the online application at http://career.cuhk.edu.hk/ and attach a letter of interest and CV. Review of applications and shortlisting will be on a rolling basis until the post is filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post via the CUHK career site. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Journalism and Communication Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001AM": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (260001AM)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (260001AM) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (260001AM) Job Description Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) - ( 260001AM ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Translation Closing date: October 31, 2026 Established in 1972, the Department of Translation of CUHK was the first of its kind in Asia. We offer a full range of BA, MA, MPhil and PhD programmes. As a historic leader in translation studies, our department is dedicated to shaping the future of a discipline in transition. Building on our robust foundation in humanities research, we aim to pioneer new approaches at the intersection of language, culture, and technology. We are currently expanding our vision beyond traditional, practical translation training, with the goal of leading the global conversation on digital multilingualism and the cultural impact of emerging language technologies. We are seeking forward-thinking scholars who possess a strong foundation in humanities research and who have (or are highly motivated to develop) an active engagement with emerging technologies. We are particularly interested in candidates whose work critically engages with how language, technology, and society intersect. Relevant areas of expertise reflect this synthesis of humanities and technology, and include, but are not limited to: AI and translation and interpreting technologies; audiovisual translation and multimodal translation; localization; and multilingual digital communication. While priority will be given to the areas listed above, applicants in all areas of translation studies who demonstrate a commitment to integrating technology and culture into their research and teaching are welcome to apply. Applicants should (i) possess a PhD degree in translation or other related fields; (ii) have relevant teaching experience and professional qualification(s); and (iii) possess a strong track record in publishing research in the field. The appointees will be expected to (a) teach undergraduate and/or postgraduate courses; (b) develop new courses in line with their own interests; (c) supervise research postgraduate students; (d) develop independent and/or collaborative research projects; and (e) undertake administrative duties. A complete application dossier should include (a) a cover letter, indicating the rank and mode of appointment you are applying for; (b) a CV, with a complete list of publications (attach the acceptance letter for an accepted but unpublished paper); (c) a research statement; (d) a teaching statement; (e) two writing samples, published or unpublished; (f) previous teaching evaluations if any; and (g) applications for assistant professors should have three confidential reference letters to be sent by the referees directly; (h) associate professor applications should include three names of referees. Except items (g) or (h), the dossiers should be submitted online at the website of Human Resources Office, the Chinese University of Hong Kong ( https://www.hro.cuhk.edu.hk/en-gb/career-opportunities ). Letters of reference should be sent directly by mail to Chairperson, Department of Translation, 1/F Leung Kau Kui Building, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shatin, N.T., Hong Kong by referees or email at tra@cuhk.edu.hk. Applicants are responsible for the completion of their application materials. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2027, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Application Procedures The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Translation Unposting Date : Oct 31, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600015R": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Business Economics) (2600015R)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Business Economics) (2600015R) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Business Economics) (2600015R) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Business Economics) - ( 2600015R ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Closing Date: December 31, 2026 The Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology comprises over 40 faculty members specializing in three research areas: Operations Management, Management Information Systems, and Business Economics. The Department now invites applications for a tenured or tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in the area of Business Economics commencing Fall 2027. Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in Economics, or related disciplines; (ii) high competence in empirical research and demonstrated research interest in, but not limited to, empirical microeconomics, macroeconomics, or health economics; and (iii) strong commitment to teaching and services. The appointee will teach undergraduate and/or postgraduate courses offered by the Department. Tenure-track appointments will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. Senior applicants for the tenured position should have an outstanding track record of research and teaching accomplishments. CUHK Business School provides internationally competitive remuneration, generous research support and funding, and relocation assistance for international faculty relocating to Hong Kong. The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific. The School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes with over 6,500 students from 30+ countries/regions, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools Accountancy Hotel & Tourism Management Departments Decisions, Operations and Technology Finance Management Marketing Application Procedure Please submit your application package (including a letter of interest, a full resume and recent teaching-related information such as teaching evaluations) via the CUHK career site and at least three reference letters should be sent directly to the Chairperson, Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology by the referees via email ( dote@cuhk.edu.hk ). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Unposting Date : Dec 31, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600015Q": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Operations Management) (2600015Q)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Operations Management) (2600015Q) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Operations Management) (2600015Q) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Operations Management) - ( 2600015Q ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Closing Date: December 31, 2026 The Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology comprises over 40 faculty members specializing in three research areas: Operations Management, Management Information Systems, and Business Economics. The Department now invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in the area of Operations Management commencing Fall 2027. Applicants for all professoriate ranks will be considered. Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in Operations Management/Operations Research, or other related disciplines (by the time reporting for duty); (ii) high competence in research and demonstrated research interest in, but not limited to, business analytics, revenue management, service operations, supply chain management; and (iii) strong commitment to teaching and services. The appointee will teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses offered by the Department. Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. Senior applicants should have an outstanding track record of research and teaching accomplishments. CUHK Business School provides internationally competitive remuneration, generous research support and funding, and relocation assistance for international faculty relocating to Hong Kong. The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific. The School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes with over 6,500 students from 30+ countries/regions, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools Accountancy Hotel & Tourism Management Departments Decisions, Operations and Technology Finance Management Marketing Application Procedure Please submit your application package (including a letter of interest, a full resume and recent teaching-related information such as teaching evaluations) via the CUHK career site and at least three reference letters should be sent directly to the Chairperson, Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology by the referees via e-mail ( dote@cuhk.edu.hk ). We will invite shortlisted candidates for in-person interviews at the INFORMS Annual Meeting (2026). Interested candidates are advised to submit the application by October 9, 2026 with information of their presentations at INFORMS, if any. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Unposting Date : Dec 31, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001C1": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001C1)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001C1) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260001C1) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 260001C1 ) Description Department/Unit: Institute of Chinese Medicine Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Institue of Chinese Medicine ( https://www.cuhk.edu.hk/icm/ ) at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is seeking exceptional applicants to join Prof. Joan Zuo’s ( https://www.cuhk.edu.hk/icm/director.html ) research team as Research Assistant Professor. The appointee will (a) apply for external competitive research grants; (b) participate and/or develop in independent and/or collaborative research projects; (c) coordinate research projects and publish peer-reviewed papers; and (d) lead the investigations from the quality control to the pharmacological and mechanistic evaluations of the herbs and herbal products, but also be able to coordinate the trials with the TCM and western physician teams on TCM products. Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in Chinese Medicine, Pharmaceutical Sciences or related discipline; (ii) substantial postdoctoral experience in a relevant scientific discipline; (iii) a strong commitment to excellence in research; (iv) ample experiences in above research area(s) as evidenced by publications in international journals; (v) a strong sense of responsibility and team spirit, and (vi) excellent oral and written communication skills. Applicants should submit an online application and attach (1) a letter of intent, and addresses how your experience matches the qualifications for the position; (2) a proposed plan of research at CUHK; (3) a complete curriculum vitae; and (4) names, addresses and contact information for at least three professional references. Candidates will be consulted before references are contacted, and all grants will be validated with the appropriate funding agency. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years commencing as soon as possible, renewable subject to good performance, funding availability and mutual agreement. The successful candidate shall be considered for potential affiliation with an academic department at CUHK. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Institute of Chinese Medicine Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001AK": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (Public History) (260001AK)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (Public History) (260001AK) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor (Public History) (260001AK) Job Description Assistant Professor (Public History) - ( 260001AK ) Description Department of History Assistant Professor (Public History) (Ref. 260001AK) (Closing Date: October 1, 2026) The Department of History at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) invites applications for a full-time, substantiation-track ( equivalent to U.S. tenure-track) position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the field of Public History, begin ning August 2, 2027. CUHK’s History Department is proud to have been the first department in the region to offer an MA in Comparative and Public History, and we have recently added a unique undergraduate stream in Public History. We seek a dynamic scholar-practitioner whose work engages with both public and scholarly audiences in innovative ways. The successful candidate will be expected to teach an introductory methodology course in Public History. In addition, their research and practice should evince a dedication to meaningful engagement with the community, governmental and non-governmental organizations, etc. (either in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People’s Republic of China or elsewhere). A track record (appropriate to career stage) of scholarly publication is expected. We welcome applicants with specialisations in any area of Public History, including (but not limited to): ·        Museum and heritage studies ·        Oral history ·        Community-engaged history ·        Digital public history ·        Archival and curatorial practice ·        Historical memory and commemoration Experience in Digital Humanities (DH) and innovative public-facing methodologies is highly desirable. The position is open to all qualified candidates, both local and international. The normal teaching load is two courses per term, reduced to one in the first term of appointment. Teaching will be conducted in English, although knowledge of Chinese will be considered an advantage. Qualifications: Applicants should: i . h old a PhD in History or a closely related field by August 1, 202 7; ii . h ave an active research agenda with clear plans for future publications ; iii . d emonstrate a commitment to teaching and mentoring students ; and iv . s how evidence of public history practice and engagement (including evidence of social impact, where appropriate) . Salary and fringe benefits for the post will be highly competitive. Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially , which, subject to funding, performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation (equivalent to U.S. tenure), either after six years of service or earlier upon special application and recommendation. Application Process Applicants should complete the online application form, upload a letter of introduction, a CV, evidence of public history practice and/or engagement with the community and one writing sample. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Shortlisted candidates will be asked to provide further materials, including letters of recommendation (to be addressed to the Department Secretary directly by the referees), evidence of teaching and public engagement experience. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of History Unposting Date : Oct 1, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260001AJ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (Ancient World History) (260001AJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (Ancient World History) (260001AJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor (Ancient World History) (260001AJ) Job Description Assistant Professor (Ancient World History) - ( 260001AJ ) Description Department of History Assistant Professor (Ancient World History) (Ref. 260001AJ ) (Closing Date: October 1, 2026) The Department of History at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) invites applications for a full-time, substantiation-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the field of Ancient World History, begin ning August 2, 2027. We welcome applicants with specialisations in areas including (but not limited to) ancient Europe, North Africa, the Middle East, and the Mediterranean world in the period c. 1000 BCE–500 CE. While chronological and thematic specialisations are open, the ability to teach ancient Greek and/or Roman history is highly desirable. The post is open to all qualified candidates, both local and international. CUHK is one of Asia’s top international research universities, ranked number #18 globally in 2027 by QS and #44 by THE . Our department has the largest cluster of World History expertise in Hong Kong and the wider region. We hope to recruit a historian who can complement and expand our existing subject coverage, helping us achieve our goal of becoming Asia’s leading centre for the study of World History. The primary language of research and instruction in World History at CUHK is English; knowledge of Chinese is not required. The successful candidate will have a strong commitment to high standards in both research and teaching. An active research agenda and clear plans for future English-language publications (including a monograph and peer-reviewed journal articles) are essential. In addition to delivering the department’s introductory survey course on Ancient World History (HIST2005), a key responsibility will be to further develop the World History curriculum, by creating new courses in line with the candidate’s interests and the department’s needs. The normal teaching load is two courses per term, reduced to one course in the first term of employment. Qualifications Applicants should: i . have obtained a doctoral degree by August 1, 2027; ii . have an active research agenda and clear plans for future English-language publications; iii . be committed to teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and iv . be ready to supervise postgraduate students. Salary and fringe benefits for the post will be highly competitive. Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which may be renewed for a further three years. Subject to funding, performance, and mutual agreement, this may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation (equivalent to U.S. tenure), either when the aggregate service period reaches six years, or sooner upon completing one year’s service, subject to special application and recommendation as appropriate. Application Process Applicants should complete the online application form, upload a letter of introduction, a CV, and one writing sample. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Shortlisted candidates will be asked to provide further materials, including letters of recommendation (to be addressed to the Department Secretary directly by the referees) and evidence of experience as both researchers and teachers. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of History Unposting Date : Oct 1, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600018S": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600018S)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600018S) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600018S) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 2600018S ) Description Prof. Barbara Chan’s lab located at the School of Biomedical Sciences (https://www2.sbs.cuhk.edu.hk) and The Institute for Tissue Engineering and Regenerative Medicine (iTERM; https://www.iterm.cuhk.edu.hk/), leads a dedicated research team focused on complex tissue engineering, biomaterials, multiphoton microfabrication and micropatterning, complex tumoroids and organoids, cell niche engineering, mechanoregulation. The School of Biomedical Sciences, Faculty of Medicine is looking for individuals to apply for the post of full-time non-clinical Research Assistant Professor. Individuals with demonstrated experience inmultiphoton microfabrication and micropatterning, biomaterials, tissue engineering and regenerative medicineCRIS are most welcome. The School will provide state-of-the-art research facilities and appropriate laboratory. Applicants should have (i) a Ph.D. or its equivalent in the biological and biomedical sciences or engineering or related disciplines; (ii) postdoctoral experiences in developing microfabrication and micropatterning technologies for biochip fabrication and cell niche studies; and (iii) a good track record of research and publication in high-impact international peer reviewed scientific journals in one or more related areas. Candidates should have excellent organizational, interpersonal and communication skills, and an excellent command of English. Active participation in interdisciplinary research is required. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for one year commencing at the fourth quarter of 2026, renewable subject to performance, funding and mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Biomedical Sciences Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600018U": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) (2600018U)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) (2600018U) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) (2600018U) Job Description Research Assistant Professor(s) - ( 2600018U ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Physics Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/are filled Post Specification: The Department of Physics at The Chinese University of Hong Kong invites applications for Research Assistant Professor positions in the field of experimental quantum sensing. Experimental Quantum Sensing : The duty of this position is to set up and develop protocols for simultaneous multi-parameter sensing (temperature, specific chemical species, pressure, current, and more) and implement time-resolved, 3D imaging of these variables with submicron spatial resolution in operating devices, using diamond NV centers and related. The applicants should have a doctoral degree with relevant research experience. Salary will be commensurate with the applicants' qualifications and experience. Appointment(s) will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Application Procedure Applicants should submit an online application and attach a full resume, research plan, teaching statement, copies of academic credentials, a publication list and/or abstracts of selected published papers (if any), together with names, addresses and fax numbers/e-mail addresses of three referees to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references (unless otherwise specified). Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Physics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000170": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (26000170)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (26000170) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant (26000170) Job Description Teaching Assistant - ( 26000170 ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Hotel and Tourism Management Closing date: Until the position is filled The School of Hotel and Tourism Management, CUHK Business School, is inviting applications for the position of Teaching Assistant. Applicants should have: (i) a good Bachelor's degree preferably in Hospitality, Business, Marketing, and Real Estate / Finance. Other majors will be considered as well; (ii) excellent communication skills in written and spoken English, as well as spoken Chinese (Cantonese and/or Mandarin); (iii) good people skill and proactive work attitude; (iv) the ability to assist in tutorials, laboratory/practical classes, compilation of course materials, and other academic activities under guidance; and (v) proficiency in Microsoft Office (e.g. Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and on-line teaching tactics. Skills in programming and using statistical software such as SPSS, R or Python and survey software such as Qualtrics will be a bonus. Relevant work experience, including internship, will also be an advantage. The appointee will support course teacher in daily pre-course planning, coordinate teaching and student related activities, perform teaching-related administrative tasks using various platforms (Blackboard, Veriguide, CATME, Mural, Socrative, Kahoot etc). He/she will also work with other administrative staff in the department to support various school events / student activities. In addition to completing the application via the CUHK Career platform with supporting documents (such as academic certificates), please upload a cover letter explaining why you are interested in this position. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for two years commencing August 2026, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Hotel and Tourism Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600016K": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600016K)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600016K) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (2600016K) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 2600016K ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Biomedical Engineering Closing Date: June 1, 2027 The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a widely accepted top institute in Asia (e.g. ranked #7 in QS Asia University Rankings 2026) with a high degree of global academic reputation (e.g. ranked #18 in QS World University Rankings 2027). The Faculty of Engineering at CUHK is famous for its research in optics and photonics, dating back to the early 1970s when Prof Charles Kao (2009 Nobel Laureate in Physics) joined CUHK. The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is the newest in the Faculty of Engineering. Still, it has already grown into global academic excellence (world #38 in 2025 Shanghai Ranking of Academic Subjects – Biomedical Engineering) and is consistently ranked No. 1 in Hong Kong. We are inviting applications for the post of Research Assistant Professor (RAP) in BME to engage in a project related to glycosaminoglycan-rich biomaterials for musculoskeletal tissue engineering applications. The project is highly interdisciplinary, involving areas of biomaterials, extracellular matrix, stem cells, mechanoregulation and musculoskeletal disorders. Opportunities for Growth The RAP position offers great opportunities for professional development, including leading independent cutting-edge research projects, mentoring postdocs and graduate students, collaborating with world-leading research groups, applying for grants and classroom teaching. Requirements Applicants should (i) possess a doctoral degree in the STEM field, such as biomedical engineering, mechanical engineering, computer engineering and applied physics; (ii) have a solid academic background in biomaterials, extracellular matrix, musculoskeletal tissue engineering and an excellent research track record; (iii) demonstrate a strong academic track record as evidenced by publishing in high-profile journals or conferences; and (iv) have proficiency in both written and spoken English. Solid postdoctoral training on carbohydrate materials is essential, but applicants with exceptional research achievements will be considered case-by-case. Experience in leading research projects independently is required, and success in research grant applications will be considered an advantage. Research Directions The RAP position is dedicated to working and developing glycosaminoglycan-rich biomaterials for musculoskeletal applications. This project is based on our prior foundation of complex extracellular matrix biomaterials for tissue engineering. Through the already-established collaboration, this study will pave the way for upcoming clinical translation in musculoskeletal tissue engineering and support the translation of Hong Kong’s scientific excellence into societal impacts. The specific aims and deliverables of research projects will be discussed with the PI, considering the applicant’s expertise, interests, and prior experience. Responsibilities The appointee’s roles and contributions include: (a) carry on the proposed project under the lead of the PI (Prof. CHAN Barbara): specifically, the appointee will (i) coordinate the GAG-rich biomaterial program; (ii) assist in mentoring RPg students working on the project; (iii) collaborate with biologists/clinicians to explore broad applications of the project; and (iv) prepare conference/journal manuscripts and drafting patents; (b) generate high-impact research outputs that are equivalent to the 4* research output in RAE: the appointee is expected to have cross-field working experience to support the multidisciplinary nature of this project; and (c) apply for external grants from RGC/NSFC/ITC/etc.: the appointee will be fostered to be an independent researcher with a good track record of securing external grants. The research results from this project are expected to strongly support the appointee in applying for and securing external grants. Salary and Contract Details Salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s qualifications and experience. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, starting as soon as possible, renewable subject to funding availability, performance and mutual agreement. How to Apply Applicants should submit an online application and attach a full resume, a list of publications, copies of academic credentials, together with names, addresses and e-mail addresses of three to five referees to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the positions are filled. Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Biomedical Engineering Unposting Date : Jun 1, 2027"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000178": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (26000178)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (26000178) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (26000178) Job Description Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) - ( 26000178 ) Description Department/ Unit: Faculty of Law Closing Date: September 15, 2026 The Faculty of Law of The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK LAW) is one of the most dynamic and accomplished research-intensive law schools in Asia. Since welcoming its inaugural student cohort in 2006, CUHK LAW has earned international recognition for excellence in legal research and education. This reputation is affirmed by the latest Research Assessment Exercise (2020) conducted by Hong Kong’s University Grants Committee, in which 83% of the Faculty’s research output was rated as “world-leading” (4*) or “internationally excellent” (3*). With a strong global outlook, our academic staff represent nearly twenty jurisdictions through their origins or training. CUHK LAW now invites applications for appointment as Professor, Associate Professor, or Assistant Professor. The Faculty upholds a robust and ambitious research culture, with research excellence firmly at the core of its academic mission. We place particular emphasis on high-quality scholarship that advances disciplinary debates and contributes meaningfully to global and regional conversations in law. Candidates for appointment at the Professor level are expected to have an established record of academic leadership in research and/or education at the international level. They should demonstrate a sustained trajectory of influential scholarship and a proven ability to mentor colleagues in advancing the Faculty’s research profile. Appointees at the Associate Professor level should have an internationally recognised reputation for research excellence and a proven capacity to contribute to the Faculty’s research profile. Candidates at this level should already possess a strong portfolio of high-impact publications and a clear scholarly agenda of continuing distinction. Candidates for Assistant Professorships should have completed their doctorate by the time of appointment and either possess a strong record of quality publications or demonstrate clear potential to develop into a productive and impactful scholar. Clear evidence of a coherent research trajectory and commitment to producing high-quality outputs will be essential. The Faculty particularly welcomes applications in foundational common law subjects (especially private law subjects), artificial intelligence and law, intellectual property law, and PRC law. Exceptionally well-qualified candidates in other areas may also be considered. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload the following documents: (a) a cover letter (maximum 2 pages); (b) a full curriculum vitae; (c) a teaching statement (maximum 2 pages); and (d) a statement of major research and scholarly achievements (maximum 3 pages), highlighting up to four representative publications or research outputs from the past five years, with a description of their originality, significance, and rigour. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis of up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. The current starting base salary, payable over 12 months,  is HK$80,825 per month (approximately US$10,350 / £7,800 per month) for Assistant Professors; HK$100,050 per month (approximately US$12,825 / £9,650 per month) for Associate Professors; and HK$126,370 per month (approximately US$16,200 / £12,190 per month) for Professors. In addition to the base salary, appointees are eligible for a monthly housing allowance and an end-of-contract gratuity, subject to prevailing terms and conditions. CUHK LAW is committed to promoting diversity and warmly welcomes applications from candidates whose backgrounds and experiences will enrich the intellectual and cultural life of the Faculty. Further information about CUHK LAW is available at http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/law . The application deadline is 15 September 2026, and applications will be considered on a rolling basis. We regret that we will only be able to contact candidates selected for further consideration. Prospective applicants are welcome to contact the Dean of the Faculty at deanoflaw@cuhk.edu.hk for informal inquiries. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Law Unposting Date : Sep 15, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600014W": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (2600014W) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (2600014W) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant - ( 2600014W ) Description Department/ Unit: The Jockey Club School of Public Health and Primary Care Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Jockey Club School of Public Health and Primary Care is a leading institution in the Asia-Pacific region, dedicated to advancing excellence in public health and primary care through innovative education, impactful research, and meaningful community engagement. The School fosters strong international partnerships with schools of public health, government bodies, and centres for disease control in Mainland China and beyond. For more information, please visit http://www.sphpc.cuhk.edu.hk . We are now seeking a motivated and forward-thinking individual to join us as a Clinical Professional Consultant in Family Medicine or Public Health Medicine. A courtesy title of Associate Professor of Practice in a related clinical specialty may be granted to appointee, subject to their professional qualifications and recognized clinical experience within the field. Applicants should possess: (i) a medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong; (ii) at least three years of relevant experience in family medicine, primary care, health services, or related fields; a recognized higher professional qualification in family medicine will be an advantage; (iii) strong strategic thinking and planning abilities, a proactive and collaborative work ethic, and well-developed problem-solving skills; (iv) experience in teaching at the tertiary level, with a passion for nurturing future healthcare professionals; and (v) professional proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese). Proficiency in Putonghua will be an advantage. The appointee will play a key role in shaping medical education and will be responsible for: (a) delivering high-quality teaching and providing student supervision; (b) contributing to and coordinating the development of innovative teaching and training curricula, with a particular focus on medical programmes; and (c) undertaking other academic and administrative duties as required. This is an excellent opportunity to contribute to a dynamic academic environment and to influence the development of future leaders in primary care and public health. The appointment will be offered on a contract basis for up to three years, commencing as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : The Jockey Club School of Public Health and Primary Care Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600011N": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor  (2600011N)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor  (2600011N) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor  (2600011N) Job Description Assistant Professor - ( 2600011N ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Hotel and Tourism Management Closing date: January 15, 2027 The School of Hotel and Tourism Management at the Business School of the Chinese University of Hong Kong is inviting applications for a tenure-track faculty position in hospitality and tourism, starting in August 2027. Applicants should be promising scholars with a PhD (by the time of reporting for duty) in hospitality and tourism or a related field. The appointees will conduct high quality research which results in publications in top-tier hospitality and tourism journals. In addition, they are expected to undertake duties to teach basic and advanced-level hospitality and tourism courses at both undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels, and to render services to the School of Hotel and Tourism Management. We welcome applications from scholars specializing in AI and machine learning, behavioral science, healthcare and aging, sports and entertainment, and related areas. Industry experience in related fields and/or grant experience is preferred. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2027, which, subject to demonstration of the requisite level of performance and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation later. About the School of Hotel and Tourism Management Established in 1998, the School of Hotel and Tourism Management is one of six departments within the CUHK Business School. Leveraging the Business School's esteemed business education, the school is dedicated to developing future leaders in the experience economy, with a focus on hospitality, tourism, and real estate. The school provides an AACSB-accredited BBA program in Hospitality and Real Estate (HRE), the first integrated undergraduate program of its kind in Asia. At the postgraduate level, it offers two MSc programmes. The MSc in Real Estate (MRE) is the only master's degree in Asia that integrates multidisciplinary research and teaching from real estate, business, and hospitality and the MSc in Leadership for Experience Economy (LEE) is the first MSc programme in the Asia-Pacific region focusing on developing competencies in inspirational leadership, investment, and innovation to drive organizational success in the emerging experience economy. In addition, the school offers the MPhil-PhD in Business Administration, specializing in Hospitality and Real Estate, preparing students for academic and research careers. Further information about the School of Hotel and Tourism Management is available at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/hotel-and-tourism-management/ About CUHK Business School The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific. The School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes with over 6,500 students from 30+ countries/regions, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools · Accountancy · Hotel & Tourism Management Departments · Decisions, Operations and Technology · Finance · Management · Marketing Application Procedure Applicants please upload the full resume with a cover letter, copies of academic credentials, publication list with abstracts of selected published papers, details of courses taught and evaluation results (if available), a research plan, a teaching statement, together with names, addresses and e-mail addresses of three referees for providing references via the CUHK e- recruitment system at http://career.cuhk.edu.hk/. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk. Deadline for Application The School will continue to review applications on a rolling basis. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for interviews in batches starting in fall 2026. Applications will be closed on 15 January 2027. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Hotel and Tourism Management Unposting Date : Jan 15, 2027"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600011M": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor  (2600011M)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor  (2600011M) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor  (2600011M) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor - ( 2600011M ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Hotel and Tourism Management Closing date: until the position is filled The School of Hotel and Tourism Management at the Business School of the Chinese University of Hong Kong is inviting applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position (at all ranks) in hospitality and tourism. Applicants should be promising or established scholars with a PhD (by the time of reporting for duty) in hospitality and tourism or a related field. The appointees will conduct high quality research which results in publications in top-tier hospitality and tourism journals. In addition, they are expected to undertake duties to teach basic and advanced-level hospitality and tourism courses at both undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels, and to render services to the School of Hotel and Tourism Management. We welcome applications from scholars specializing in hospitality and tourism management and related fields. For those applying for the Associate or Full professor rank, preferred candidates will have industry experience, expertise in program development and/or executive education, a proven track record in grants, contracts, or consultancy, along with demonstrated academic leadership. Appointment at Assistant Professor rank will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2027, which, subject to demonstration of the requisite level of performance and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Outstanding candidates with substantial experience for Professor rank may be considered for substantive appointment forthwith. The rank and exact start date will be subject to negotiation. About the School of Hotel and Tourism Management Established in 1998, the School of Hotel and Tourism Management is one of six departments within the CUHK Business School. Leveraging the Business School's esteemed business education, the school is dedicated to developing future leaders in the experience economy, with a focus on hospitality, tourism, and real estate. The school provides an AACSB-accredited BBA program in Hospitality and Real Estate (HRE), the first integrated undergraduate program of its kind in Asia. At the postgraduate level, it offers two MSc programmes. The MSc in Real Estate (MRE) is the only master's degree in Asia that integrates multidisciplinary research and teaching from real estate, business, and hospitality and the MSc in Leadership for Experience Economy (LEE) is the first MSc programme in the Asia-Pacific region focusing on developing competencies in inspirational leadership, investment, and innovation to drive organizational success in the emerging experience economy.  In addition, the school offers the MPhil-PhD in Business Administration, specializing in Hospitality and Real Estate, preparing students for academic and research careers. Further information about the School of Hotel and Tourism Management at CUHK is available at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/hotel-and-tourism-management/ About CUHK Business School The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific. The School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes with over 6,500 students from 30+ countries/regions, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools · Accountancy · Hotel & Tourism Management Departments · Decisions, Operations and Technology · Finance · Management · Marketing Application Procedure Applicants please upload the full resume with a cover letter, copies of academic credentials, publication list with abstracts of selected published papers, details of courses taught and evaluation results (if available), a research plan, a teaching statement, together with names, addresses and e-mail addresses of three referees for providing references via the CUHK e- recruitment system at http://career.cuhk.edu.hk/. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk. Deadline for Application The School will continue to review applications on a rolling basis. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for interviews in batches starting in fall 2026 and continuing until the position is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Hotel and Tourism Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600014Z": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (2600014Z)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (2600014Z) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant (2600014Z) Job Description Teaching Assistant - ( 2600014Z ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Mathematics Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Department of Mathematics invites applications for the post of full-time Teaching Assistant. Applicants should have (i) a good Bachelor's degree and preferably some relevant teaching experience; (ii) an academic background in mathematics; (iii) solid knowledge of computer applications and project management; and (iv) good communication skills. Duties include (a) handling coordination work, including teaching support and programme administration; (b) assisting in tutorials, laboratory/practical classes, preparation of course materials/classes, student consultation/supervision, and other academic activities; and (c) assisting in report drafting and writing. Appointments will be made on a contract basis up to two years commencing as soon as possible and renewable subject to funding, performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Mathematics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600011X": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Management Information Systems) (2600011X)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Management Information Systems) (2600011X) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Management Information Systems) (2600011X) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Management Information Systems) - ( 2600011X ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Closing Date: February 28, 2027 The Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology comprises over 40 faculty members specializing in three research areas: Operations Management, Management Information Systems, and Business Economics. The Department now invites applications for multiple tenure-track faculty positions in the area of Management Information Systems commencing Fall 2027. Applicants for all professoriate ranks will be considered. Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, or related disciplines (by the time reporting for duty); (ii) competence in high-quality research in information systems; and (iii) strong commitment to teaching and services. Senior applicants should have an outstanding track record of research and teaching accomplishments. The appointee(s) will teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses offered by the Department. Appointments will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. CUHK Business School provides internationally competitive remuneration, generous research support and funding, and relocation assistance for international faculty relocating to Hong Kong. About CUHK Business School CUHK Business School is a world-leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific. The Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (MBA, MSc, EMBA, DBA, MPhil, PhD) with over 6,500 students, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools Accountancy Hotel & Tourism Management Departments Decisions, Operations and Technology Finance Management Marketing Application Procedure Please submit your application package (including a letter of interest and a full resume) via the CUHK career site. Other information (e.g., teaching evaluations and reference letters) may be requested at a later stage. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for Zoom interviews and/ or in-person interviews at conferences (e.g., AMCIS'26, CIST’26 or ICIS’26). Applications will be processed on a rolling basis. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Unposting Date : Feb 28, 2027"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600013K": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (2600013K)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (2600013K) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (2600013K) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor - ( 2600013K ) Description Department of Psychology Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (Ref. 2600013K) Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Department is keen to enhance its reputation as a world-class research hub and generator of knowledge that prides itself over teaching and mentorship. It hopes that new faculty members will embrace that agenda with the support of abundant facilities at the Department. The Department is seeking a quality scholar with proven research excellence in any subfield of Psychology . Applicants should have (i) demonstrated potential/ ability to build a strong publication track record and obtain grants; (ii) international experience; and (iii) strong commitment to supervise students. Scholars with demonstrated academic leadership, research excellence, a track record of obtaining external competitive funding and rich experience in student’ supervision are particularly welcome . The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (e.g. research methods); (b) supervise students’ projects and theses; (c) undertake research; and (d) assist in service and administrative duties. The appointee at Professor rank will also play a leadership role in teaching and research initiatives and administrative services. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2027, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Outstanding candidates with substantial experience for Professor rank may be specially considered for appointment on substantive basis forthwith. Salary and fringe benefits will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The University offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package, including medical care, a contract-completion gratuity for an appointment of two years or longer, and housing benefits for eligible appointee. The terms mentioned herein are for reference only and are subject to revision by the University. Further information about the Department and its programmes is available at http://www.psy.cuhk.edu.hk . For enquiries, please contact the Department via e-mail at infopsy@cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Psychology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000YI": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (260000YI)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (260000YI) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (260000YI) Job Description Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors - ( 260000YI ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Accountancy Closing Date: Until the positions are filled Join Our Dynamic Faculty at the School of Accountancy The School of Accountancy at the CUHK Business School is now inviting applications for the positions of Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors, commencing duty in July-August 2027. Applications from qualified scholars in all specialty areas of accounting (including financial accounting, managerial accounting, auditing, taxation, accounting information systems) or information technology related to business applications will be considered. Applicants should have a doctoral degree (or one that is close to completion) in accounting, finance, or economics. The appointee will be required to teach postgraduate and undergraduate accounting or accounting program-related courses and will be expected to publish in top-tier accounting/finance journals. For assistant professor positions, appointments will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, which subject to demonstration of the requisite level of performance and mutual agreement may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation (tenure) later. Salary, teaching load and faculty support are comparable to that of top US business schools and based on qualifications. A research start-up fund will be provided to support the appointees’ research general expenses and research support staff. Attractive Compensation and Benefits We offer globally competitive salaries and compensation packages commensurate with qualifications, comparable to that offered by top US business schools. In addition, our faculty members enjoy the following benefits: · Housing Benefits : Housing benefits will be provided where applicable, ensuring a seamless transition to Hong Kong. · Contract End Gratuity : Assistant professor appointees will be entitled to receive a contract end gratuity upon completion of the entire term of contract, rewarding the dedication and long-term commitment. · Medical Benefits and Relocation Allowances : We provide comprehensive medical benefits coverage to the appointee and his/her spouse & dependent children (if applicable) and relocation allowances for eligible new appointees recruited from outside Hong Kong. · Low Tax Rate : The effective income tax rate in Hong Kong is a maximum of 15 percent, allowing you to make the most of your earnings. About the School of Accountancy The School of Accountancy at CUHK Business School is a renowned institution that has consistently demonstrated research excellence and is ranked among the top schools worldwide in terms of research strength. The School offers four highly attractive and competitive programmes: · BBA in Professional Accountancy (PACC) – Focusing on globally oriented accounting skills, this programme is ideal for aspiring professional accountants or specialists in an accounting-related area. · Master of Accountancy (MAcc) – This programme provides students with the conceptual and practical accounting knowledge to generate valuable business insights. · Executive Master of Professional Accountancy with SNAI (EMPAcc) – Jointly offered with Shanghai National Accounting Institute (SNAI), this programme focuses on the latest developments in accounting and finance. · MPhil-PhD in Accountancy – This programme focuses on theoretical and applied accounting research with an interdisciplinary thrust including statistical decision theory and law. For more detailed information about the School and the faculty’s research, please visit our website at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/accountancy/ . About CUHK Business School CUHK Business School is a world-leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained global recognition for nurturing business leaders with immense success and contributions. The Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (DBA, MBA, MSc, EMBA, MPhil, PhD) with over 6,500 students, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: • Schools · Accountancy · Hotel & Tourism Management • Departments · Finance · Decisions, Operations, and Technology · Management · Marketing Application Procedure Applicants should submit the application package online via the CUHK career site and upload a full resume, a job-market paper, and other publications or working papers. Additionally, we require three letters of recommendation, which should be sent directly by the referees to the School of Accountancy by e-mail at schoolacy@cuhk.edu.hk . The School of Accountancy will interview shortlisted candidates on a timely basis. Join us at the School of Accountancy, CUHK Business School, and become part of a vibrant and intellectually stimulating academic community. Together, let's shape the future of accounting education and research. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Accountancy Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000X9": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) (260000X9)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) (260000X9) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) (260000X9) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) - ( 260000X9 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Management Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Management at the CUHK Business School is now inviting applications for faculty position(s) at the Professor/ Associate Professor levels commencing in 202 7 . Applications are invited from qualified scholars with expertise in macro management (e.g., strategy, innovation, entrepreneurship, international business, family business, sustainability, etc.) or micro management (e.g., organizational behavior, leadership, human resource management, etc.). Applicants should possess (i) a PhD degree in management or a related discipline; (ii) excellent teaching performance, particularly in delivering graduate courses; (iii) a sound track record of publications in top-tier journals; and (iv) strong commitment to service at Faculty and Departmental levels. The appointee(s) will teach courses mainly at the graduate level, such as MBA, EMBA, DBA and MSc courses; publish high-quality scholarly research; and participate in academic and professional activities. He/she is expected to actively bid for competitive external funding support for research endeavors. Appointment will commence in 202 7 . Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Salary and Fringe Benefits Salary will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The University offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package, including medical care and housing benefits for eligible appointee(s). About the Department of Management The Department of Management offers three specialized concentrations in Entrepreneurship (ENT), Human Resource Management (HRM), and Management of International Business (MIB) in the Integrated BBA Programme, and two Master’s Programmes in Management and Sustainable Global Business. Our competitive curriculum equips students with cutting-edge knowledge in management, a global outlook, an innovative spirit, and a strong sense of social responsibility and integrity, enabling future business leaders to lead transformative initiatives worldwide. For more information about the Department, please visit our website at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/management/ . About CUHK Business School The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in the Asia Pacific. The Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (MBA, MSc, MAcc, EMBA, DBA, MPhil, PhD) with over 6,500 students from 30+ countries/regions, as well as executive education programmes. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 4 9 ,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools - Accountancy - Hotel & Tourism Management Departments - Finance - Decisions, Operations and Technology - Management - Marketing Application Procedure Applicants should submit the application package online via the CUHK career site (including a completed on-line application form, full resume, publication list, and evidence of teaching excellence, if any), and provide names and email addresses of at least three referees for providing reference. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Review of applications will be conducted on a rolling basis and will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. For enquiries, please contact the Department of Management via mgt@cuhk.edu.hk . Interested scholars are welcome to connect with Department colleagues at upcoming major conferences to learn more about the Department. These include the 2026 AOM Conference (Philadelphia, US), the Department’s AOM Reception (Philadelphia Marriott Downtown, evening of 2 August), and the 2026 AIB Conference (Manchester, UK). Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000XA": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor(s) (260000XA)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor(s) (260000XA) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor(s) (260000XA) Job Description Assistant Professor(s) - ( 260000XA ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Management Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Management at the CUHK Business School is now inviting applications for the tenure-track position(s) at the Assistant Professor level. We welcome applications from both fresh PhD graduates and seasoned Assistant Professors who are engaged in high-quality scholarship specialized in macro management areas (e.g., strategy, innovation, entrepreneurship, international business, family business, sustainability, etc.) or micro management areas (e.g., organizational behavior, leadership, human resource management, etc.). Applicants should possess a PhD degree in management or a related discipline; have a publication record commensurate with the years of experience; and be strongly committed to excellence in scholarly research, teaching and service. Responsibilities include publishing high-quality scholarly research; teaching management courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels; and participating in academic and professional activities. The appointee(s) is/are also encouraged to apply for external funding to support research endeavors. Salary and Fringe Benefits Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing in 202 7 , which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Salary will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The University offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package, including medical care and housing benefits for eligible appointee(s). About the Department of Management The Department of Management offers three specialized concentrations in Entrepreneurship (ENT), Human Resource Management (HRM), and Management of International Business (MIB) in the Integrated BBA Programme, and two Master’s Programmes in Management and Sustainable Global Business. Our competitive curriculum equips students with cutting-edge knowledge in management, a global outlook, an innovative spirit, and a strong sense of social responsibility and integrity, enabling future business leaders to lead transformative initiatives worldwide. For more information about the Department, please visit our website at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/management/ . About CUHK Business School The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong, China. Since its establishment in Hong Kong, China in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in the Asia Pacific. The Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (MBA, MSc, MAcc, EMBA, DBA, MPhill, PhD) with over 6,500 students from 30+ countries/regions, as well as executive education programmes. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 49,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools - Accountancy - Hotel & Tourism Management Departments - Finance - Decisions, Operations and Technology - Management - Marketing Application Procedure Applicants should submit the application package online via the CUHK career site (including s completed on-line application form, full resume, publication list, and evidence of teaching excellence, if any), and provide names and email addresses of at least three referees for providing reference. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Review of applications will be conducted on a rolling basis and will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. For enquiries, please contact the Department of Management via mgt@cuhk.edu.hk . Interested scholars are welcome to connect with Department colleagues at upcoming major conferences to learn more about the Department. These include the 2026 AOM Conference (Philadelphia, US), the Department’s AOM Reception (Philadelphia Marriott Downtown, August 2, 2026), and the 2026 AIB Conference (Manchester, UK). Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000Z0": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s)  (260000Z0)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s)  (260000Z0) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s)  (260000Z0) Job Description Professor(s) - ( 260000Z0 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Microbiology Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Microbiology, The Chinese University of Hong Kong is seeking full-time academic staff at the rank of Professor. The Department has a wide range of research facilities, with access to a large comprehensive teaching hospital.  The establishment provides a good environment for basic as well as clinical research and facilitates collaboration with other disciplines. Further information about the department is available at http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/med/mic/ . Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree or equivalent; (ii) a strong research track record in the field of microbiology; and (iii) commitment to undergraduate teaching and postgraduate student supervision. Applicants should also have a strong record of external funding support, international recognition and leadership. Experience in microbial biology, translational microbiome research, bioinformatics and systems microbiology is an advantage. The appointee(s) will (a) undertake teaching and related educational activities for undergraduate and postgraduate students; (b) supervise MPhil and PhD students; (c) apply for competitive research grants and related funding; and (d) conduct high-standard research projects independently and in collaboration with other parties. Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing as soon as possible, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Microbiology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000W0": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (260000W0)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (260000W0) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (260000W0) Job Description Teaching Assistant(s) - ( 260000W0 ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Accountancy Closing Date: Until the post is filled The School of Accountancy of The Chinese University of Hong Kong is now inviting applications for the position of Teaching Assistant for its undergraduate and master programmes. Applicants should have a Bachelor's Degree or a Master’s Degree in accounting and demonstrate a strong eagerness to learn new topics in data analytics and AI applications. In addition, applicants should have (i) good command of written and spoken English, (ii) good presentation skills; (iii) a meticulous attitude, a strong sense of responsibility as well as good interpersonal skills; and (iv) willingness to work under pressure. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for interview. The appointee will assist professors and lecturers in lectures, tutorials, preparing course materials, grading, student consultation, examination invigilation and other academic activities as assigned. He/she will also work with other administrative staff in the School to support various events / student activities. The appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to mutual agreement and good performance. We offer a highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. This position provides an excellent opportunity to gain practical experience and develop academic skills, which could enhance a candidate’s eligibility for more advanced teaching support roles within the School of Accountancy in the future. Application Procedure Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date resume, academic transcripts and other relevant information to the system. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Non-local applicants are welcome, and CUHK will assist and support with the working visa application process. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Accountancy Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000S0": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Professional Consultant(s) (260000S0) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professional Consultant(s) (260000S0) Job Description Professional Consultant(s) - ( 260000S0 ) Description Department/ Unit: Faculty of Law Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Faculty of Law at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK LAW) is among the most dynamic and accomplished law schools in Asia. Since welcoming its inaugural cohort in 2006, CUHK LAW has experienced remarkable growth, both in scale and international stature. With a strong global outlook, our academic staff represent nearly twenty jurisdictions through their origins or training. CUHK LAW is now inviting applications for appointment(s) as Professional Consultant(s). Professional Consultants primarily focus on teaching courses in the Postgraduate Certificate in Laws (PCLL) programme, as well as core and elective common law subjects in the LLB, JD, and LLM programmes. Applicants should possess: (i) a law degree from a recognized university and/or a relevant professional qualification for legal practice; (ii) at least two years of post-qualification experience as a solicitor or barrister in Hong Kong, or its equivalent in another common law jurisdiction; and (iii) experience in teaching law or demonstrable aptitude for legal education. Candidates with expertise in the following areas are of particular interest: Writing and Drafting Commercial Documents (English and Chinese), Commercial Practice, China Practice, and Banking and Finance. Applications from highly qualified individuals with other areas of expertise may also be considered. The appointee(s) will perform duties assigned by the Faculty Dean, including but not limited to: (a) teaching at the CUHK Graduate Law Centre in Central and the CUHK campus in Shatin; (b) contributing to curriculum development and supporting programme administration; (c) serving as academic advisor(s) to students; and (d) undertaking administrative duties and providing service to CUHK LAW, the College, and/or the University, as appropriate. The appointment(s) will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to mutual agreement and satisfactory performance. Applicants are required to complete the online application form and upload the following documents: a full curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy and/or methodology (maximum 2 pages); copies of qualification documents; and contact details of three referees who have agreed to provide references. Applicants with current or prior law school teaching experience should also include teaching evaluations. All applications will be treated with the strictest confidence. CUHK LAW is firmly committed to fostering diversity and warmly encourages applications from candidates whose backgrounds and experiences will enrich the diversity of our faculty. Further details about CUHK LAW can be found at http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/law . Applications will be considered on a rolling basis until the relevant teaching needs of the Faculty have been met. We regret that we will only be able to contact candidates selected for further consideration. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Law Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000RI": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor (260000RI)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor (260000RI) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor (260000RI) Job Description Professor - ( 260000RI ) Description Department/ Unit: Faculty of Social Science Closing date: Until the post is filled The Faculty of Social Science invites applications for the post of Professor. The appointee will be expected to serve as the inaugural Director for the new inter-Faculty undergraduate programme in Diplomacy and International Studies at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK). This innovative programme aims to nurture high-level, interdisciplinary talent who are proficient in both Chinese and Western cultures and are prepared to excel in international relations, international organizations and diplomatic arenas. With a particular focus on China’s role in global governance, the programme sees to students’ developing a deep understanding of the historical, cultural, and political dimensions of China’s engagement in international affairs. The Faculty is seeking a visionary leader with demonstrated commitment to teaching, programme management, and the development of this distinctive new initiative. For more details about the programme, please visit: https://socsc.cuhk.edu.hk/diplomacy-and-international-studies/introduction/ . The appointee will be responsible for: (a) leading the development and continuous improvement of the new inter-Faculty undergraduate programme in meeting international standards; (b) fostering interdisciplinary collaborations to ensure the development of and adherence to the international standards in research and teaching; (c) providing leadership and strategic direction in alignment with the academic missions of CUHK and the participating Faculties; and (d) enhancing global connections in the field of international studies and diplomacy. Applicants are expected to have: (i) a PhD degree in International Relations/International Law or related disciplines; (ii) a distinguished record of academic achievements and international recognition in research, scholarship and teaching; (iii) proven record of leadership and extensive administrative experience at senior levels, preferably in a prominent research institution; (iv) demonstrated ability to foster interdisciplinary collaboration; and (v) strong international network and experience in programme development. Appointment is targeted to start in August 2026 or as soon as practicable thereafter. Outstanding candidate may be specially considered for substantive appointment forthwith. Application Procedure To apply for the post, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, CV, teaching statement, research statement, representative research outputs, and past teaching performance records. Review of applications will commence from mid-May 2026. Applications will be considered until the post is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Social Science Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000RK": {
      "title": "Job Description - Lecturer (260000RK)",
      "description": "Job Description - Lecturer (260000RK) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Lecturer (260000RK) Job Description Lecturer - ( 260000RK ) Description Department/ Unit: Faculty of Social Science Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Faculty of Social Science invites applications for a post at Lecturer rank for the new inter-Faculty undergraduate programme in Diplomacy and International Studies at The Chinese University of Hong Kong. This innovative programme aims to nurture high-level, interdisciplinary talent who are proficient in both Chinese and Western cultures and are prepared to excel in international relations, international organizations and diplomatic arenas. With a particular focus on China’s role in global governance, the programme sees to students’ developing a deep understanding of the historical, cultural, and political dimensions of China’s engagement in international affairs. For more details about the programme, please visit: https://socsc.cuhk.edu.hk/diplomacy-and-international-studies/introduction/ . The appointee will be responsible for: (a) supporting the development and continuous improvement of the new inter-Faculty undergraduate programme in meeting international standards; (b) teaching and supporting curriculum design in areas such as international relations, international law and related disciplines; and (c) coordinating programme administration, student advising, and collaborative activities with various programme partners/ stakeholders. Applicants are expected to: (i) have a PhD degree in International Relations/ International Law or related disciplines; (ii) possess teaching experience in international relations, international law or related disciplines; and (iii) be committed to and experienced in interdisciplinary collaboration, curriculum innovation, and student engagement. Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to two years initially, targeted to start in August 2026 or as soon as practicable thereafter, renewable subject to performance, funding availability, and mutual agreement. Application Procedure To apply for the post, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, CV, teaching statement, past teaching performance records (if applicable), together with two reference letters. Review of applications will commence from mid-May 2026. Applications will be considered until the post is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Social Science Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000SF": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260000SF)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260000SF) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260000SF) Job Description Teaching Assistant - ( 260000SF ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Sports Science and Physical Education Closing Date: Until the position is filled Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor’s degree in physical education and sports science or related disciplines; and (ii) at least 2 years’ school teaching and/or sports-related administrative experience. The appointee will (a) provide academic support and guidance for student elite athletes; (b) assist in internship coordination and supervision; and (c) assist in teaching-related academic activities as assigned. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Sports Science and Physical Education Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000TM": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260000TM)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260000TM) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (260000TM) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 260000TM ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Closing Date: Until the position is filled Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in biological sciences or related disciplines; and (ii) demonstrated research ability and experience in cell biology, molecular biology, patient derived cancer models for personalized therapy, anti-cancer drug studies (in-vitro and in-vivo) or other advanced techniques such as next-generation sequencing (NGS). Applicants with at least 4 years of relevant postdoctoral experience and a strong publication record are preferred. Track records in gaining competitive research grant and experiences in breast cancer research would be an advantage. The appointee is expected to (a) seek external grants; (b) carry out cancer-related research; (c) co-supervise students; and (d) assist in laboratory management. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings: (i) full resume; (ii) copies of academic credentials; (iii) full publication list; and (iv) names and e-mail addresses of three to five referees to whom the applicant's consent has been given for their providing reference. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000PY": {
      "title": "Job Description - Part-time Instructor(s) (Cantonese) (260000PY)",
      "description": "Job Description - Part-time Instructor(s) (Cantonese) (260000PY) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Instructor(s) (Cantonese) (260000PY) Job Description Part-time Instructor(s) (Cantonese) - ( 260000PY ) Description Yale-China Chinese Language Academy Part-time Instructors (Cantonese) (Ref: 260000PY) Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled Yale-China Chinese Language Academy is recruiting Part-time Instructor(s) for its University Programme Section. Classes will mainly be conducted on weekdays from 8:30 a.m. to 6:15 p.m. Applicants should (i) hold a relevant bachelor’s degree or higher in applied linguistics, Chinese language and literature, language education, or another relevant field; (ii) speak fluent Cantonese and have high proficiency in written and spoken English; (iii) be familiar with the language teaching pedagogy; (iv) be familiar with and able to use online teaching software and teaching platforms. Applicants with teaching experience in higher education institutions will be given priority. [Applicants who have previously applied for the same position (Job No. 26000055) are not required to apply again.] 雅禮中國語文研習所 兼任導師（粵語） 雅禮中國語文研習所現正為其大學課程部招聘兼職導師。課程主要於平日上午八時三十分至下午六時十五分進行。 應徵者須具備以下條件： (i) 持有應用語言學、中國語言文學、語言教學等相關學士或以上學位； (ii) 精通粵語，有良好英語表達能力； (iii) 熟悉語言教學法； (iv) 熟練使用網絡教學軟件及電子教學平臺。具有高等教育院校教學經驗者可獲優先考慮。 [ 曾申請相同職位（職位編號： 26000055 ）的人士毋須再次提交申請。 ] Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Yale-China Chinese Language Centre Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000RT": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Professional Consultant(s) (Full-time/ Fractional-time) (260000RT) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professional Consultant(s) (Full-time/ Fractional-time) (260000RT) Job Description Professional Consultant(s) (Full-time/ Fractional-time) - ( 260000RT ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Management Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Management at the CUHK Business School is now inviting applications for the position(s) of Full-time/Fractional-time Professional Consultant. We welcome applications from the qualified scholars in the management fields, including but not limited to family business management, leadership, innovation management, entrepreneurship, organizational behaviour, s trategic management , etc. Applicants should have (i) a higher degree, preferably a DBA or PhD in any business or other related disciplines from a recognized university; (ii) substantial and extensive professional experience in managing organizations, preferably at senior level; (iii) a strong and proven track record in teaching executive and master’s degree program me s (e.g. MBA , EMBA); and (iv) impressive academic/ professional records. The appointee is expected to deliver high-quality teaching primarily for executive and master’s degree programmes and probably for some undergraduate courses as well ; assume administrative roles and responsibilities in the prgoramme/course levels, as assigned ; coordinate learning activities such as internships and study tours; and contribute to enhancing the programme quality and reputation. The initial appointment will be made on a full-time/ fractional-time contract basis for two years commencing in 2026 , renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Salary and Fringe Benefits Salary will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The University offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package including medical care for eligible appointees. About the Department of Management The Department of Management offers three specialised concentrations in Entrepreneurship (ENT), Human Resource Management (HRM), and Management of International Business (MIB) in the Integrated BBA Programme, and two Master’s Programmes in Management and Sustainable Global Business. Our competitive curriculum equips students with cutting-edge knowledge in management, a global outlook, an innovative spirit, and a strong sense of social responsibility and integrity, enabling future business leaders to lead transformative initiatives worldwide. For more information about the Department, please visit our website at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/management/ . About CUHK Business School The CUHK Business School is a leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong , China . Since its establishment in Hong Kong , China in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in the Asia Pacific. The Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (DBA, MBA, MSc, MAcc, EMBA, PhD) with over 5,0 00 students from 3 0+ countries/regions, as well as executive education programmes. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 4 9 ,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: Schools - Accountancy - Hotel & Tourism Management Departments - Finance - Decisions, Operations and Technology - Management - Marketing Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. Please also include your full resume,  evidence of teaching ability, names and email addresses of at least three referees for providing confidential reference for your application. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Review of applications will be conducted on a rolling basis and will continue until the position(s) is/ are filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000KJ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor  (260000KJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor  (260000KJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor  (260000KJ) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 260000KJ ) Description School of Architecture Research Assistant Professor (Ref. 260000KJ) (Closing Date: Until the post is filled) The Chinese University of Hong Kong is one of the world’s leading universities, ranked at 37 th place internationally and ranked No. 1 in Hong Kong in the recently released Best Global Universities Rankings 2025 by the U.S. News & World Report. Its location makes it one of the most exciting places to research on and teach architecture. The School of Architecture has a world-class, research-led and professionally connected learning environment. It embraces new approaches to architectural education and cross-disciplinary research that impact society and profession. The School has an ambitious growth plan and is now seeking outstanding candidates to make significant contributions to both diversify its portfolio and support its existing strengths in architectural scholarship. The appointee will drive forward a research agenda related to the School’s strategic areas and develop research collaborations within the University and beyond. He/ She will be a key player in the research team working on environmental studies led by Prof essor Edward Ng. Applicants should have a doctoral degree in a subject area relevant to Statistics, Public Health, or related disciplines, with at least two years of postdoctoral research experience in environmental or urban climate studies. Preference will be given to candidates with a strong research and practical record in the following areas: Impact assessment of climate change on urban and built environment Measurement and modeling of climate vulnerability in urban designs Risk analysis of climate-related hazards within high-density and complex settings Application of advanced modeling technologies for climate and health impact evaluation Development of strategies to enhance the resilience of urban structures and communities against extreme weather events Applicants should have good proposal and report writing, communication and interpersonal skills.  Applicants should have a good scholarly record demonstrating research excellence. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in research grant application and project management. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. To apply for the post, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, a full CV, a research statement, together with names/e-mail addresses of three referees with consent for providing references. Salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s qualifications and experience. The CUHK School of Architecture is actively building a more diverse and inclusive environment. Qualified individuals from underrepresented sections of society are encouraged to apply. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. To explore the School and the post further, please visit https://www.arch.cuhk.edu.hk/people/careers .  Enquiries may be directed to Ms. Tammy Kong, School Manager at arc.appointment@cuhk.edu.hk . Review of applications and shortlisting will start in June/July 2026 until the post is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Architecture Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000I9": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (Sustainable and Environmental Design) (260000I9)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (Sustainable and Environmental Design) (260000I9) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (Sustainable and Environmental Design) (260000I9) Job Description Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (Sustainable and Environmental Design) - ( 260000I9 ) Description School of Architecture Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor ( Sustainable and Environmental Design ) (Ref. 260000I9) (Closing Date: Until the post is filled) The Chinese University of Hong Kong is one of the world’s leading universities. Its location makes it one of the most exciting places to research on and teach architecture. The School of Architecture has a world-class, research-led and professionally connected learning environment. It embraces new approaches to architectural education and cross-disciplinary research that impact society and profession. The School has an ambitious growth plan and is seeking an outstanding candidate to lead the development in the area of Sustainable and Environmental Design . The appointees will drive forward a research agenda and deliver teaching for undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, while building research collaborations within the University and beyond. Applicants should (i) have a PhD degree in a subject area relevant to architecture or urbanism;  (ii) strong commitment to excellence in research and teaching; and (iii) outstanding accomplishments and research potential. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing July / August 2027, which, subject to performance, funding availability and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Outstanding candidates with substantial experience for Professor rank may be specially considered for appointment on substantive basis forthwith. To apply for the posts, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, CV, teaching statement, research statement, portfolio, together with names and e-mail addresses of three referees with consent for providing references. Appointment level and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s qualifications and experience. The CUHK School of Architecture is actively building a more diverse and inclusive environment. Qualified individuals from underrepresented sections of society are encouraged to apply. To explore the School and the posts further, please visit our website at https://www.arch.cuhk.edu.hk/people/careers . Enquiries may be directed to Ms. Tammy Kong, School Manager at arc.appointment@cuhk.edu.hk . Review of applications and shortlisting will start in May 2026 until the post is filled. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Architecture Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000I1": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Professor(s) (260000I1)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Professor(s) (260000I1) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Professor(s) (260000I1) Job Description Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Professor(s) - ( 260000I1 ) Description Department/ Unit: Faculty of Medicine Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/ are filled Faculty Global Talent Recruitment Scheme About the Faculty of Medicine The motto of the Faculty of Medicine at CUHK is 'Transforming our Passion into Perfection'. The Faculty, established in 1981, now comprises 19 teaching departments/schools/units covering the entire range of pre-clinical and clinical disciplines, including the School of Biomedical Sciences, The Nethersole School of Nursing, the School of Pharmacy and The Jockey Club School of Public Health and Primary Care. Its teaching hospital, Prince of Wales Hospital, provides more than 1,900 hospital beds and is also home to numerous medical and clinical research activities. With a team of around 1,500 full-time teaching and research staff and the back-up of the teaching hospital, the Faculty offers courses in 8 undergraduate programmes and around 60 postgraduate study programmes. The Faculty of Medicine also provides continuing and professional training for public health and healthcare professionals. In 2024-25, the numbers of undergraduate and postgraduate research students in the Faculty have reached 3,600 and 700 respectively. About the Scheme The Faculty of Medicine is now inviting applications under the Faculty Global Talent Recruitment Scheme. We welcome global talents with strong potential for scientific and scholarly breakthroughs across all disciplines to join us as Research Assistant Professors, Assistant Professors, Associate Professors, and Professors. Further information about the Faculty Global Talent Recruitment Scheme is available at https://www.med.cuhk.edu.hk/about-us/career . Strategic Recruitment Areas Applications are especially encouraged from scholars in the following priority areas: · Infectious Diseases · Academic Breast Surgery · Cardiovascular Science · Neuroscience · Advanced Cell Therapies and Novel Oncological Treatments · Chemical Engineering for New Drug Discovery and Development · Artificial Intelligence in Medicine Competitive Compensation and Benefits Successful applicants under the Faculty Global Talent Recruitment Scheme will be offered a competitive compensation package, including start-up support, relocation support and other benefits such as housing allowance, annual leave, academic leave, medical benefits and retirement benefits. Requirement and Application Procedures Applicants for non-clinical positions should be holders of PhD degree. For clinical positions, applicants should have a medical qualification, preferably with a higher medical qualification in the relevant discipline. Please send in applications via the e-recruitment system. Your application should include: · Cover Letter (Specifying the position applied for and your Department/School/Unit of interest) · Curriculum Vitae · Research & Teaching Statements · Three Key Publications The search will go on until the best candidates are presented for decision. The University reserves the right to fill the posts by invitation. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Medicine Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=230001J4": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor (230001J4)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor (230001J4) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor (230001J4) Job Description Professor/ Associate Professor - ( 230001J4 ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Architecture Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Chinese University of Hong Kong is one of the world’s leading universities, ranked at 53rd place internationally and ranked No. 1 in Hong Kong in the recently released Best Global Universities Rankings 2023 by the U.S. News & World Report. Its location makes it one of the most exciting places to research on and teach architecture. The School of Architecture has a world-class, research-led and professionally connected learning environment. It embraces new approaches to architectural education and cross-disciplinary research that impact on the society and profession. The School has an ambitious growth plan and is seeking an outstanding candidate to lead the development in the area of Sustainable and Environmental Design . The appointees will drive forward a research agenda and deliver teaching for undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, while building research collaborations within the University and beyond. Applicants should (i) have a PhD degree in a subject area relevant to architecture or urbanism and (ii) have ideally more than 10 years of post-PhD experience. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years commencing July / August 2024, which, subject to performance, funding availability and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Outstanding candidates would be considered for substantive appointment. To apply for the post, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, CV, teaching statement, research statement, portfolio, together with names/e-mail addresses of three referees with consent for providing references. Appointment level and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s qualifications and experience. The CUHK School of Architecture is actively building a more diverse and inclusive environment. Qualified individuals from underrepresented sections of society are encouraged to apply. To explore the School and the post further, please visit our website at https://www.arch.cuhk.edu.hk/people/careers . Enquiries may be directed to Ms. Sylvia Kwok, School Manager at arc.appointment@cuhk.edu.hk. Review of applications and shortlisting will start on 1 September 2023 until the post is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Architecture Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000DJ": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (260000DJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (260000DJ) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant - ( 260000DJ ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Closing Date: Until the post is filled Applicant should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) a specialist qualification in obstetrics and gynaecology; (iii) experience in teaching medical students; and (iv) a track record of research. The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (b) provide clinical service; and (c) assist in clinical research. Appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000BX": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (260000BX)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (260000BX) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (260000BX) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) - ( 260000BX ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Electronic Engineering Closing Date: Until the position(s) is / are filled About the Department of Electronic Engineering The Department of Electronic Engineering (EE) was established in 1970 by Professor Charles K. Kao, a 2009 Nobel laureate in Physics, and offers full‐spectrum programs from Bachelor’s, research and taught Master’s degrees to PhD degree. For detailed information about the Department, please visit our departmental website at http://www.ee.cuhk.edu.hk/ . Research Fields The research fields of the Department cover bioelectronics and medical devices, robotics and sensor technology, pattern recognition and artificial intelligence, signal, speech and image processing, data science and machine learning, antenna and propagation, radio frequency (RF) / microwave engineering and wireless communications, photonics and optical communications, quantum technology, solid-state electronics and VLSI, and power electronics and green technology. Requirements The Department has planned to recruit several positions and invites highly motivated and highly qualified candidates to apply for positions at the Professor, Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level. The applicants must have a PhD degree in EE or closely related fields. Preference will be given to those with expertise in integrated circuit design, RF/microwave engineering, quantum engineering or quantum information science. Candidates with exceptional qualifications in other related research fields will also be considered. The successful applicants are expected to establish themselves as international leaders in their fields of research, to teach with passion at both undergraduate and graduate levels, and to take on service and administrative duties. Application Procedures Please submit application online and upload the following documents: a) full resume; b) copies of academic credentials; c) publication list with soft copies of 5 most representative publications; d) details of courses taught and evaluation results (if available); e) a research plan; f) a teaching statement; and g) the names and contact information of three to five referees. Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. The start date is flexible and can be arranged with the successful applicants. Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Applications will be accepted until the position(s) is/are filled. We reserve the right to fill the positions by invitation or not to fill the positions. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Electronic Engineering Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=260000C5": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260000C5)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260000C5) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant (260000C5) Job Description Teaching Assistant - ( 260000C5 ) Description Department of Psychology Teaching Assistant (Ref: 260000C5) Closing Date: Until the post(s) is / are filled. Applicants should have (i) a Master’s, MPhil or PhD Degree in Psychology, preferably in Industrial-Organizational Psychology; (ii) demonstrated ability or experience to support the teaching of courses in the area of Industrial-Organizational Psychology; and (iii) proficiency in statistical analysis to provide support on student projects; (iv) proficient in both English and Chinese, and proficiency in spoken Cantonese or Putonghua is preferred. Duties include assisting in (a) coordinating academic activities; (b) reviewing coursework assignments; (c) guiding student projects, (d) facilitating classroom discussions; and (e) performing other administrative tasks, such as managing program admissions, preparing program reports, and organizing program events, as assigned by supervisors. The role requires attending classes on weekday evenings and occasionally on weekends, subject to special teaching arrangements. Appointment will initially be made on a 2-year contract with contract-end gratuity, starting in August. The contract is renewable, subject to good performance and mutual agreement. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Psychology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600006V": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor  (2600006V)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor  (2600006V) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor  (2600006V) Job Description Assistant Professor - ( 2600006V ) Description Department/Unit: School of Pharmacy Closing Date: Until the post is filled School of Pharmacy at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) invites applications for a tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor.   We seek a highly motivated and collaborative scholar with a research focus that advances the fields of health economics, pharmacoepidemiology, medication safety, real-world data science, pharmacogenomics, or pharmacovigilance. This position offers an outstanding opportunity to develop an independent, externally funded research program within a vibrant academic community. The successful candidate will contribute to the School’s mission of improving patient care and public health through innovative research and education. Responsibilities: The appointee is expected to: (a) develop and maintain an independent, rigorous, and externally funded research programme; (b) publish scholarly work in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals; (c) contribute to the teaching mission of the School by instructing professional (Bachelor of Pharmacy) and graduate (Master of Clinical Pharmacy, MPhil and PhD in Pharmacy) students in relevant areas; (d) mentor graduate students and postdoctoral fellows; (e) provide service to the School, College, University, and the broader professional community; and (f) other academic and professional duties assigned by the School Director. Required Qualifications: Applicants should have: (i) a PharmD, PhD, or equivalent doctoral degree in pharmacoeconomics, pharmacoepidemiology, health outcomes research, pharmaceutical sciences, public health, or a closely related discipline; (ii) a strong record of scholarly achievement, demonstrated by publications in peer-reviewed journals relevant to the stated research fields; (iii) evidence of potential to secure independent external research funding; (iv) excellent written and verbal communication skills; and (v) a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring a diverse body of students. Preferred Qualifications: Applicants with the following will have an advantage: (i)  postdoctoral research experience or equivalent; (ii)  a proven record of, or strong potential for, interdisciplinary collaboration; and (iii) experience in teaching or teaching assistant role in the pharmacy-related fields at the university level. Review of applications will commence in February 2026 and continue until the post is filled. Candidates will be contacted before references being approached, and all grants will be validated with the appropriate funding agency. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. For enquiries, please contact: pharmacy@cuhk.edu.hk About the School: The School of Pharmacy CUHK is a leader in pharmaceutical education, research, and practice. Our faculty members are at the forefront of discovery in drug development, clinical pharmacy, and population-based health sciences. We offer state-of-the-art research facilities, a supportive collegial environment, and strong collaborative ties with our academic medical center, other health science schools, and regional healthcare systems. For more information about our School's education programmes and research, please visit School's website https://www.pharmacy.cuhk.edu.hk . Application Procedure: To apply, please submit an online application with the following attachments: 1) a cover letter addressing qualifications and alignment with the position; 2) a statement of research interest and future plan (max 3 pages); 3) a statement of your teaching philosophy and experience (max 2 pages); 4) a comprehensive curriculum vitae; and 5) contact details for at least three professional references. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Pharmacy Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600007E": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical) (2600007E)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical) (2600007E) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical) (2600007E) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical) - ( 2600007E ) Description Department/Unit: Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Closing Date: December 31, 2026 The Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK), is an academic department based at the Prince of Wales Hospital (PWH), a 1,637-bed tertiary referral teaching hospital. The hospital provides a wide range of acute specialist services, including stroke, obstetric, cardiac and trauma centres. The clinical service provides anaesthesia for 14,000 operations in the main operating theatres, with one third being emergency cases, with an additional 2000 anaesthetics are administered in other areas. The 26-bed adult intensive care unit provides medical and surgical critical care for approximately 1800 patients per year. The department is committed to achieving excellence in education and research and maintains active educational and research collaborations with numerous international and mainland institutions. Applicants should have: (i) a specialist medical qualification in Anaesthesia and/or Intensive Care (approved for specialist registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) at least 3 years of relevant experience in anaesthesia and/or intensive care; and (iii) a good command of spoken and written English. Proficiency in Cantonese and Putonghua will be an advantage, but not essential. Duties include: (a) providing high quality clinical services in anaesthesia and/or intensive care; (b) student supervision and teaching undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (c) clinical research, and (d) other duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Applicants with a plan to pursue a higher degree in anaesthesia/intensive care and/or education will be encouraged and supported. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, commencing as soon as possible. Subject to performance and mutual agreement, this may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Unposting Date : Dec 31, 2026"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600004S": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Curriculum Studies (2600004S)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Curriculum Studies (2600004S) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Curriculum Studies (2600004S) Job Description Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Curriculum Studies - ( 2600004S ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Closing Date: Until the position is filled The Department of Curriculum and Instruction under the Faculty of Education at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a dynamic centre in the Asia-Pacific region for teaching and research in the broad areas of curriculum and instruction. In addition to Faculty-based undergraduate teacher education, Postgraduate Diploma in Education, Master of Education, Doctor of Education and PhD programmes, the Department offers several Master of Arts/ Science programmes as well as research supervision across a range of subject areas. The Faculty of Education of CUHK is an international centre for professional training and research in education. Detailed information about the Faculty of Education and the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/ . The Department now invites applications for full-time appointment as Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Curriculum Studies. Applicants should have (i) excellent academic qualifications including a relevant doctoral degree; (ii) a strong commitment to excellent teaching; and (iii) a track record of active research and publications. The ability to teach cross-disciplinary courses will be advantageous. Applicants for appointment as Associate Professor should have a track record of outstanding research and publications, as well as success in obtaining competitive research grants. They should also demonstrate strong scholarship with an international impact, evidenced by invitations to present at major international academic meetings, and experience in supervising research postgraduate students. The appointee will (a) teach and design courses related to curriculum development, instructional design, and learning sciences in primary and secondary schools; (b) undertake scholarly research and seek external competitive research grants; (c) conduct teaching practicum supervision; (d) supervise postgraduate students; and (e) direct and manage programmes. Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to funding and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Review of applications will start on March 30, 2026. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Curriculum and Instruction Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600004T": {
      "title": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Curriculum Studies (2600004T)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Curriculum Studies (2600004T) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Curriculum Studies (2600004T) Job Description Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Curriculum Studies - ( 2600004T ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Closing Date: Until the position is filled The Department of Curriculum and Instruction under the Faculty of Education at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a dynamic centre in the Asia-Pacific region for teaching and research in the broad areas of curriculum and instruction. In addition to Faculty-based undergraduate teacher education, Postgraduate Diploma in Education, Master of Education, Doctor of Education and PhD programmes, the Department offers several Master of Arts/ Science programmes as well as research supervision across a range of subject areas. The Faculty of Education of CUHK is an international centre for professional training and research in education. Detailed information about the Faculty of Education and the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/ . The Department invites applications for a full-time appointment as Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Curriculum Studies. For Senior Lecturer, applicants should have (i) a relevant doctoral degree; and (ii) at least 8 years of post-doctoral relevant experience. Evidence of research and scholarly activities is also generally expected. For Lecturer, applicants should have (i) a Master’s degree (preferably a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline); and (ii) at least 4 years of post-Master relevant experience. Applicants who possess a doctoral degree with less experience will also be considered. Applicants should also have (a) a strong track record in teaching; (b) extensive professional experience, leadership services to schools and the education community; (c) good knowledge of the education systems of Hong Kong and its neighbouring communities; and (d) strong commitment to excellence in teaching. A good track record of pedagogical research and an initial record of refereed publications are added advantages. The appointee will be responsible for curriculum development and teaching teacher education and higher degree programmes offered by the Faculty of Education. Supervision of teaching practice is also required. Appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for up to two years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Review of applications will start on March 16, 2026. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Curriculum and Instruction Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000010": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical)  (26000010)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical)  (26000010) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical)  (26000010) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Clinical) - ( 26000010 ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Surgery Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/are filled Founded in 1982, the Department of Surgery focuses on excellence in clinical work and scholarly research, with a strong commitment to education and training. Over the past decades, these values have been at the core of our academic activities. Located within the Prince of Wales Hospital, the Department of surgery offers opportunities in clinical and laboratory research in basic sciences as well as biomedical engineering. We are committed to improving care for our patients through research in clinical outcomes and have been at the forefront of both endoscopy and laparoscopy technology. We are looking for candidates who can contribute to the continuous growth of the Department. Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (preferably approved for full registration with the Medical Council of Hong Kong; other qualifications would be considered on a case-by-case basis); (ii) a fellowship of the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine or equivalent and a specialist registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong; (iii) post-qualification experience in relevant discipline, i.e. General Surgery/ Breast Surgery/ Plastic Surgery/ Paediatric Surgery/ Urology/ Neurosurgery/ Cardiothoracic Surgery; and (iv) an outstanding track record and accomplishments in teaching, clinical services and research. The appointee(s) will (a) provide clinical services; (b) conduct research and clinical trials; (c) undertake teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels ; and (d) undertake administrative duties in the Department, Faculty and University. The appointee(s) will work mainly at the Prince of Wales Hospital and hospitals in the New Territories East Cluster. Further information about the scope of services provided by the Department is available at https://www.surgery.cuhk.edu.hk/ Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and approval, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Surgery Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000011": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Research Assistant Professor(s) (Non-clinical)  (26000011)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Research Assistant Professor(s) (Non-clinical)  (26000011) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Research Assistant Professor(s) (Non-clinical)  (26000011) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) / Research Assistant Professor(s) (Non-clinical) - ( 26000011 ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Surgery Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/are filled Founded in 1982, the Department of Surgery focuses on excellence in clinical work and scholarly research, with a strong commitment to education and training. Over the past decades, these values have been at the core of our academic activities. Located within the Prince of Wales Hospital, the Department of surgery offers opportunities in clinical and laboratory research in basic sciences as well as biomedical engineering. We are committed to improving care for our patients through research in clinical outcomes and have been at the forefront of both endoscopy and laparoscopy technology. We are looking for candidates who can contribute to the continuous growth of the Department. Applicants should have (i) a doctoral degree; (ii) substantial postdoctoral experience in the following research area(s): oncology research, biomedical research, surgical sciences,  mechatronics engineering or related disciplines; (iii) strong research accomplishments in grants and publications; (iv) active involvement in writing grant proposals; (v) the potential to become an independent researcher in obtaining future/sustained extramural funding as principal investigator and establishing significant externally-funded research programmes; (vi) a strong sense of responsibility and team spirit; (vii) capability to mentor postgraduate students and junior researchers; and (viii) an excellent command of both Chinese and English. The appointee(s) will (a) work closely with faculty members in the Department in translational research; (b) conduct research in the identified research area, generate high impact research papers and secure extramural funding; (c) undertake teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and (d) undertake administrative duties in the Department, Faculty and University. Further information about the scope of services provided by the Department is available at https://www.surgery.cuhk.edu.hk/ Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and approval, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation [for Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) only]. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Surgery Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2600002B": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor/ Research Assistant Professor (2600002B)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor/ Research Assistant Professor (2600002B) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor/ Research Assistant Professor (2600002B) Job Description Assistant Professor/ Research Assistant Professor - ( 2600002B ) Description Department/ Unit: The Nethersole School of Nursing Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Nethersole School of Nursing, formerly the Department of Nursing, was established in the Faculty of Medicine in 1991. The School is committed to excellence in teaching, research and in the promotion of the highest standards of nursing practice. Further information about the School is available at http://www.nur.cuhk.edu.hk/ . Assistant Professor Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in nursing or a related discipline; (ii) experience in tertiary-level research and teaching; and (iii) a research record demonstrated by publishing papers in refereed journals. Substantial publications in international journals and a record of award of competitive research grants will be advantageous. Research Assistant Professor Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in nursing or a related discipline; (ii) strong academic credentials and outstanding academic records; (iii) firm commitment in good quality teaching and research; and (iv) a research record demonstrated by publishing papers in high-impact refereed journals.  Applicants with collaborative research projects involving different disciplines will have an advantage. The appointee will be expected to (a) apply for external competitive research grants; (b) develop and participate in collaborative research projects; (c) supervise postgraduate students; (d) teach courses at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; (e) take up research administrative duties of the School; and (f) perform other duties as assigned by the Director or his delegates. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings: 1.    full resume; 2.    copies of academic credentials; 3.    full publication list, with web link of the papers; 4.    three recent publication samples; 5.    a statement of research interest; 6.    citations (Google or ISI); 7.    an indication, in %, the share of contributions among authors of a publication; 8.    evidence of teaching performance, if any; and 9.   names and e-mails addresses of three referees to whom the applicant's consent has been given for providing reference (unless otherwise specified). Appointment of Assistant Professor will normally be made on contract basis for two years initially commencing as soon as possible, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Appointment of Research Assistant Professor will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years commencing as soon as possible, renewable subject to good performance, funding availability and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : The Nethersole School of Nursing Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000004": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (26000004)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (26000004) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor (26000004) Job Description Assistant Professor - ( 26000004 ) Description Department/ Unit: Faculty of Social Science Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Gender Studies Programme at The Chinese University of Hong Kong is the ﬁrst programme in gender studies in the tertiary education sector in Hong Kong. It is an interdisciplinary unit based in the Faculty of Social Science, oﬀering Bachelor, MA, MPhil and PhD programmes. The forward-looking team of Gender Studies Programme is inviting applications for the post of Assistant Professor on substantiation (tenure) track to join from the academic year 2026-27 or as soon as possible. The appointee is expected to (a)    conduct research and secure research grants; (b)    teach courses at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (c)    supervise students’ theses; and (d)    undertake administrative duties. Applicants should possess: (i)     a PhD degree by the time of reporting for duty; (ii)    relevant research experience in gender/sex/sexuality-related areas; (iii)   demonstrated potential/ ability for high quality research; and (iv)   a strong sense of responsibility and commitment to excellent research, teaching, and service. Applicants specializing in any of the following areas are preferred: •    Empirical gender/sex/sexuality studies •    ⁠Human and social development •    Social sustainability or sustainable development Applicants who specialize in a subject field in Social Science (e.g., Journalism, Social Work, Political Science, Economics) that adds to the diversity of the existing team or whose profile strengthens the programme’s internationalization are preferred. Applicants in cognate subjects (e.g., Education) will also be considered if they possess a profile of a good match to Social Science and especially if they are strong in quantitative empirical research. Application Procedure Candidates should complete and submit the online application form with the following documents/information: (a)    latest CV; (b)    a cover letter; (c)    a research statement; (d)    two sample publications; (e)    a teaching statement; (f)     copies of academic credentials and relevant certificates; (g)    names and contact information of three referees; and (h)    evidence of teaching performance, if applicable. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to mutual agreement, and may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. Review of applications will start in April 2026 and continue until the post is filled. For more information about the programme, please visit: https://www.gender.cuhk.edu.hk/ . For initial enquiries, please contact Ms. Winnie Ling of the programme (email: winnieling@cuhk.edu.hk ). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Social Science Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500024B": {
      "title": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Science Education (2500024B)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Science Education (2500024B) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Science Education (2500024B) Job Description Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Science Education - ( 2500024B ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Closing Date: Until the position is filled The Department of Curriculum and Instruction under the Faculty of Education at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a dynamic centre in the Asia-Pacific region for teaching and research in the broad areas of curriculum and instruction. In addition to Faculty-based undergraduate teacher education, Postgraduate Diploma in Education, Master of Education, Doctor of Education and PhD programmes, the Department offers several Master of Arts / Science programmes as well as research supervision across a range of subject areas. The Faculty of Education of CUHK is an international centre for professional training and research in education. Detailed information about the Faculty of Education and the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/ . The Department invites applications for full-time appointment as Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer in Science Education. For Senior Lecturer, applicants should have (i) a relevant doctoral degree; and (ii) at least 8 years of post-doctoral relevant experience. Evidence of research and scholarly activities is also generally expected. For Lecturer, applicants should have (i) a Master’s degree (preferably a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline); and (ii) at least 4 years of post-Master relevant experience. Applicants who possess a doctoral degree with less experience will also be considered. Applicants should also have (a) a strong track record in teaching; (b) extensive professional experience, leadership services to schools and the education community; (c) good knowledge of the education systems of Hong Kong and its neighbouring communities; and (d) strong commitment to excellence in teaching. A good track record of pedagogical research, an initial record of refereed publications, and the ability to contribute to the teaching and development of courses related to educational technology and/or STEAM education are added advantages. The appointee will be responsible for curriculum development and teaching in teacher education and higher degree programmes offered by the Faculty of Education. Supervision of teaching practice is also required. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Review of applications will start on February 1, 2026. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Curriculum and Instruction Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500024A": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Science Education (2500024A)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Science Education (2500024A) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Science Education (2500024A) Job Description Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Science Education - ( 2500024A ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Closing Date: Until the position is filled The Department of Curriculum and Instruction under the Faculty of Education at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a dynamic centre in the Asia-Pacific region for teaching and research in the broad areas of curriculum and instruction. In addition to Faculty-based undergraduate teacher education, Postgraduate Diploma in Education, Master of Education, Doctor of Education and PhD programmes, the Department offers several Master of Arts/ Science programmes as well as research supervision across a range of subject areas. The Faculty of Education of CUHK is an international centre for professional training and research in education. Detailed information about the Faculty of Education and the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/ . The Department now invites applications for full-time appointment as Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor in Science Education. Applicants should have (i) excellent academic qualifications including a relevant doctoral degree; (ii) a strong commitment to excellent teaching; and (iii) a track record of active research and publications. Ability to teach courses related to educational technology and/or STEAM education will be advantageous . Applicants for appointment as Associate Professor should have a track record of outstanding research and publications, as well as success in obtaining competitive research grants. They should also demonstrate strong scholarship with an international impact, evidenced by invitations to speak at major international academic meetings, and experience in supervising research postgraduate students. The appointee will (a) teach and design courses related to science teaching in primary and secondary schools; (b) undertake scholarly research and seek external competitive research grants; (c) conduct teaching practicum supervision; (d) supervise postgraduate students; and (e) direct and manage programmes. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to funding and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. Review of applications will start on February 1, 2026. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Curriculum and Instruction Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=25000216": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor and Chairperson,  Department of Educational Administration and Policy (25000216)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor and Chairperson,  Department of Educational Administration and Policy (25000216) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor and Chairperson,  Department of Educational Administration and Policy (25000216) Job Description Professor/ Associate Professor and Chairperson,  Department of Educational Administration and Policy - ( 25000216 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Educational Administration and Policy Closing date: Until the position is filled The Department of Educational Administration and Policy now seeks to appoint distinguished scholar as Department Chairperson. An academic appointment will be made at Professor or Associate Professor level on substantiative (tenured) or contract basis concurrently subject to the appointee’s credentials. Applicants from the areas of Educational Leadership and Administration or Foundations in Education and Policy Studies in Education are welcome. As one of the four academic departments under the Faculty of Education at CUHK ( www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk ), the Department is part of an internationally recognized center for professional training and research in education. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/eap . Applicants should have (i) excellent academic qualifications including a doctoral degree in educational administration, leadership, policy studies, early childhood education, ethics for teaching profession,  sociology of education, philosophy of education, artificial intelligence in education or a related discipline; (ii) proven leadership experience in tertiary education institution(s); (iii) a strong research background in areas that will contribute or enhance the existing strengths of the Department; (iv) a track record of programmatic research and publications; and (v) strong commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship. For appointment at Professor level, applicants should demonstrate a strong record of professional achievement and visibility. The appointee will be required to: (a) Provide visionary leadership in formulating and implementing the Department’s long-term strategies and plans, ensuring alignment with the University’s Strategic Plan. Foster a culture of excellence by mentoring and empowering team members to achieve objectives efficiently and to world-class standards; (b) Promote and support innovative, high-impact research, and actively encourage interdisciplinary and interdepartmental collaboration; (c) Ensure the delivery of high-quality teaching across undergraduate, postgraduate, and professional programmes; and (d) Lead efforts to build and strengthen strategic partnerships with leading tertiary institutions, creating opportunities for collaboration in education, research, and knowledge transfer. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Applicants may consider their applications unsuccessful if they are not invited for an interview within 6 months after application. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Educational Administration and Policy Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000U3": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor (250000U3)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor (250000U3) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor (250000U3) Job Description Associate Professor - ( 250000U3 ) Description Department of Social Work Associate Professor (Ref. 250000U3) ( Closing Date: Until the post (s) is / are filled .) As a world-leading centre of social work education and research, the Department is dedicated to developing and disseminating scientific rigorous and socially impactful social work knowledge for human betterment and social development. We aspire, through our research and evaluation work, to improve the lives of vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, deepen our understanding of social issues and promote evidence-based practice locally and globally. The Department is looking for candidates who embrace these goals and values. Scholars specializing in any of the following research areas are welcome to apply for the post s : -          clinical social work -          children and family -          gerontology -          macro social work theories and practice Applicants should have (i) a relevant PhD degree; (ii) a strong publication track record; (iii) proven ability to obtain grants and conduct research to generate academic and social impact; (iv) demonstrated academic leadership; and (v) evidence of outstanding teaching performance. Being registered social workers and having professional expertise or substantial work experience in clinical or macro social work practice will be added assets. The appointees will ( a ) undertake research; ( b ) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; ( c ) supervise research postgraduate students; and ( d ) take up key administrative roles for the Department. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Social Work Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001ZC": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (250001ZC)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (250001ZC) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (250001ZC) Job Description Professors / Associate Professors / Assistant Professors - ( 250001ZC ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Information Engineering Closing Date: Until the posts are filled The Department of Information Engineering (IE) has multiple tenure-track faculty openings at the levels of Professor, Associate Professor, and Assistant Professor. In particular, we are looking for strong candidates in the areas of artificial intelligence (broadly defined), internet of things (broadly defined), and optical communications (design and experimental research of the next-generation optical fiber transmission/access networks, optical-wireless terrestrial/underwater systems, etc.). We will also consider outstanding candidates in other areas of information engineering to supplement our existing strength in communication systems, networking, information theory, security, and deep learning research. Further information about the Department can be found at http://www.ie.cuhk.edu.hk . Applicants should have (i) a relevant PhD degree; (ii) strong commitment to excellence in research and teaching; and (iii) outstanding accomplishments and research potential. Appointments will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2026, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Applicants please upload the full resume with a cover letter, copies of academic credentials, publication list with abstracts of selected published papers, a research plan, a teaching statement, together with names and email addresses of three to five referees to whom consent has been given for their providing reference (unless otherwise specified). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Information Engineering Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001W2": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (250001W2)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (250001W2) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (250001W2) Job Description Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor - ( 250001W2 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Sociology Closing Date: Until the post is filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. The Department of Sociology has a diverse international community, featuring academic staff and postgraduate students from six continents and fourteen countries over the past five years. In recent years, the Department has gained significant recognition in academic circles, ranking 18th globally in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subject. This achievement reaffirms our leadership position and highlights our commitment to academic excellence and impactful research. The Department of Sociology is now inviting applications for a tenure-track faculty post at Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor rank. Applicants should have (i) a relevant PhD degree by the time of employment; and (ii) a proven record of academic scholarship and (iii) high potential for excellence in teaching and research. Applicants specializing in any of the following three areas are preferred: •    Economic sociology •    Social sustainability •    Digital sociology and technology The appointee will be responsible for (a) teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b) supervising research students; (c) undertaking scholarly research; (d) applying for competitive research grants; and (e) assisting in administrative work. Salary and Fringe Benefits Appointment will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation. Outstanding candidates with substantial experience for Professor rank may be specially considered for appointment on substantive basis forthwith. The remuneration package will be highly competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. The University offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package, including medical care and housing benefits for eligible appointees. Application Procedure Please submit the online application form, a letter of interest, CV, teaching statement, research statement, a publication list, and/or abstracts of selected published papers, together with names/e-mail addresses of three referees with consent for providing references. Consideration of applications will continue until the post is filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Sociology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001UP": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor(s) (250001UP)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor(s) (250001UP) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor(s) (250001UP) Job Description Assistant Professor(s) - ( 250001UP ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Physics Closing date: Until the post(s) is/ are filled The Department invites applications for tenure-track Assistant Professor positions (either theoretical or experimental). The Department anticipates filling two positions in the following fields which are immediately available until filled: - Quantum information science (including quantum AI) - Quantum computing and related quantum technologies - Materials for quantum technology While the appointment(s) is/ are expected at the Assistant Professor level, more senior appointment(s) will be considered for candidates with exceptional qualifications. Applicants should (i) have a relevant PhD degree with postdoctoral research experience; (ii) demonstrate a track record of research accomplishments and potential for establishing a significant externally funded research program; and (iii) have a strong interest in teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment(s) or substantiation. Application Procedure Applicants should submit an online application and attach a full resume, research plan, teaching statement, copies of academic credentials, a publication list and/ or abstracts of selected published papers (if any), together with names, addresses and fax numbers/ e-mail addresses of three referees to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references (unless otherwise specified). Applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Physics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001SJ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250001SJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250001SJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250001SJ) Job Description Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors - ( 250001SJ ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Mathematics Closing date: Until the posts are filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. The Department of Mathematics in CUHK has developed a strong reputation in teaching and research. Many of the faculty members are internationally renowned and are recipients of prestigious awards and honours. The graduates are successful in both academia and industry. The Department is highly ranked internationally, e.g., it is 66th, 63rd and 42nd in the 2023, 2024 and 2025 QS World University Rankings, and 42nd, 56th and 51st in the 2023, 2024 and 2025 US News Rankings, respectively. The Department is now inviting applications for substantiable-track faculty posts at all the academic levels, with the opportunity for a joint appointment between the Department and The Institute of Mathematical Sciences. Applicants should have (i) a relevant PhD degree in mathematics or related disciplines; (ii) an established track record in research, including publications; and (iii) a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2026, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to substantiation or longer-term appointment later. Applicants please upload a full resume and attach copies of academic credentials, together with names and e-mail addresses of at least four referees (at least three on research and one on teaching) to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2025 and will continue until the positions are filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Mathematics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001TJ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s) (250001TJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s) (250001TJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s) (250001TJ) Job Description Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s) - ( 250001TJ ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Finance Closing Date: Until the position(s) are filled The Department of Finance at CUHK Business School now invites applications for the positions of Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s). We welcome applications from qualified scholars specializing in all areas of finance. The Department of Finance currently has 44 full-time faculty members, with 3/4 of them being tenured and tenure-track faculty in different areas of finance.  The Department has been expanding in recent years and is on upward trajectory in research productivity, with many faculty members successfully publishing in Journal of Finance, Journal of Financial Economics, Review of Financial Studies, Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis, among others. The CUHK was ranked 36 th globally and 2 nd in the Asia-Pacific region in the UT Dallas World Business School Research Ranking based on the publications in the three finance top-tier journals (JF, JFE, RFS) from 2019-2024. For appointment at the rank of Associate Professor, candidates should have excellent track record of publications at the very best journals and demonstrable teaching performance. For appointment at the rank of Professor, they should also demonstrate strong record of professional achievement and visibility.  For either appointment, candidates are expected to provide leadership to help the Department to grow, and teach in the more demanding postgraduate programmes (MSc/MBA/EMBA/PhD). For more detailed information about the Department and the faculty research, please visit our websites at https://www.bschool.cuhk.edu.hk/departments/finance and https://www.cuhk.edu.hk/fin/research/top-publications.pdf respectively. About CUHK Business School CUHK Business School is a world-leading business school and a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific. CUHK Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (MBA, MSc, EMBA, DBA, MPhil, PhD) with over 5,000 students, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 45,000 alumni around the world. It comprises two Schools and four Departments: o  Schools •   Accountancy •   Hotel & Tourism Management o  Departments •   Decisions, Operations & Technology •   Finance •   Management •   Marketing Application Procedures Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload a curriculum vitae at https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001TJ . The recruitment committee will follow up and may request additional information or schedule an online meeting if required. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Finance Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001SK": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professors (250001SK)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professors (250001SK) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professors (250001SK) Job Description Research Assistant Professors - ( 250001SK ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Mathematics Closing date: Until the posts are filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. The Department of Mathematics in CUHK has developed a strong reputation in teaching and research. Many of the faculty members are internationally renowned and are recipients of prestigious awards and honours. The graduates are successful in both academia and industry. The Department is highly ranked internationally, e.g., it is 66th, 63rd and 42nd in the 2023, 2024 and 2025 QS World University Rankings, and 42nd, 56th and 51st in the 2023, 2024 and 2025 US News Rankings, respectively. The Department has multiple openings for Research Assistant Professors. The Department is now cordially inviting applications for non-substantiable posts at Research Assistant Professor level in all areas of Mathematics. We seek promising young mathematicians whose research areas match the areas of our faculty members. Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in mathematics or related disciplines; and (ii) demonstrated potential for research and teaching. The main duties of the appointees will focus on research. They are also expected to undertake light teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, with one course each academic year. Appointments will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years commencing August 2026, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Applicants please upload a full resume and attach copies of academic credentials, together with names and e-mail addresses of at least four referees (at least three on research and one on teaching) to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2025 and will continue until the positions are filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Mathematics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001RA": {
      "title": "Job Description - Lecturer (250001RA)",
      "description": "Job Description - Lecturer (250001RA) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Lecturer (250001RA) Job Description Lecturer - ( 250001RA ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Sociology Closing date: Until the post is filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. The Department of Sociology has a diverse international community, featuring academic staff and postgraduate students from six continents and fourteen countries over the past five years. In recent years, the Department has gained significant recognition in academic circles, ranking 18th globally in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subject. This achievement reaffirms its leadership position and highlights its commitment to academic excellence and impactful research. The Department of Sociology is now inviting applications for a post of Lecturer. Applicants should have (i) a doctoral degree in sociology; (ii) relevant teaching experience; and (iii) demonstrated potential for effective teaching (at the undergraduate and Master programme level) in digital society and artificial intelligence, and/or sociology of media and culture. Preference will be given to applicants with teaching expertise in the following areas: sociology of technology, sociology of work and organisations, media and society, sociological theory, or a broad range of subfields. The appointee is expected to also participate/provide service in departmental teaching development, community liaison, and other academic activities. The appointment will be made on a contract basis for one to two years, targeted to start in August 2026 or as soon as practicable thereafter, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Screening of applications will be conducted on an ongoing basis until the post is filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Sociology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001QO": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Clinical) (250001QO)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Clinical) (250001QO) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Clinical) (250001QO) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Clinical) - ( 250001QO ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Closing Date: Until the position is filled Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for full or limited registration with the Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) training in histopathology (Anatomical Pathology); (iii) a higher qualification [MRCPath, FRCPA, FRCP(C), Diploma of American Board of Pathology (AP), or FHKAM(Pathology)]; (iv) subspecialty experience in Anatomical Pathology / Renal Pathology; and (v) a significant track record of research and publication in Anatomical Pathology / Renal Pathology. The appointee is expected to contribute to teaching, research and service for the Department. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings: (i) full resume; (ii) copies of academic credentials; and (iii) full publication list. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/med/acp . For enquiries, please contact Professor Gary TSE, Chairperson of the Department (e-mail: garytse@cuhk.edu.hk ). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001PQ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (250001PQ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (250001PQ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professors / Assistant Professors (250001PQ) Job Description Associate Professors / Assistant Professors - ( 250001PQ ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Statistics and Data Science Closing Date: Until the posts are filled The Department of Statistics and Data Science at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) was founded in 1982. We have strived to provide students state-of-the-art statistical education as well as to conduct cutting-edge statistical research. The Department has accommodated world-class faculty members with diverse research areas including statistical finance and risk management science, statistical theory and methodology, machine learning & big data analytics, biostatistics and bioinformatics, and other areas of cross-disciplinary research. Various research fundings and equipment would be offered by the Department for enhancing teaching and research. The Department and CUHK are committed to inclusive excellence and actively promote the success of a diverse population of students, staff, and faculty. We strive to recruit and retain a diverse community of scholars, and welcome applicants whose experience in teaching, research, or community service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to diversity. Applications are invited for two tenured or tenure -track faculty position s at the level of Associate Professor / Assistant Professor for all areas of Statistics and Data Science . (Department’s strategic areas: http://www.sta.cuhk.edu.hk/research/#dos-tab1 ). The appointment rank will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful candidate . Applicants should have (i) a Ph.D. degree in statistics or a related field; and (ii) high-quality research output and a strong teaching track record. Applicants with international exposure / background are highly preferred. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing in Fall 2026 or beyond, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointments or substantiation later. Further information about the competitive compensation and benefits, together with numerous supports on research and teaching could be found: https://www.hro.cuhk.edu.hk/en-gb/career/working-cuhk . Application review will be commenced once application is received and will continue until the posts are filled. The Global STEM Professorship Scheme is opened for application on a regular basis. We welcome distinguished scholars for applications and nominations (at the academic level of Professor or above). Please contact the Department (statdept@cuhk.edu.hk) directly for details. Further information on the Department of Statistics and Data Science can be found at http://www.sta.cuhk.edu.hk . Application Procedure Applicants please complete the online application form and upload a cover letter, a full curriculum vitae, a statement of research and teaching interests, and copies of up to five recent publications. Applicants should also provide names, addresses and e-mail addresses of three referees to whom the applicants’ consent has been given for their providing references. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the posts above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Statistics and Data Science Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001QP": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant(s) (250001QP) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant(s) (250001QP) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant(s) - ( 250001QP ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Closing Date: Until the positions are filled Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) a higher qualification [MRCPath/ FRCPA/ FRCP(C)/ Diploma of American Board of Pathology(AP)/ FHKAM(Pathology) or equivalent]; (iii) at least six years’ post-internship experience; and (iv) experience in medical teaching and clinical services in surgical pathology. Duties include (a) participating in related clinical activities; (b) providing guidance and consultation to trainees in the Department; (c) teaching undergraduate and postgraduate programmes; and (d) planning and organizing professional educational activities. Appointment(s) will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subjec t to performance and mut ual agreement. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings: (i) full resume; (ii) copies of academic credentials; (iii) full publication list; and (iv) names and e-mail addresses of three to five referees to whom the applicant's consent has been given for their providing reference. For enquiries, please contact Professor Gary Tse, Chairperson of the Department (e-mail: garytse@cuhk.edu.hk ). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001QM": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (250001QM)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (250001QM) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (250001QM) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor - ( 250001QM ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Closing Date: Until the position is filled Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree with postdoctoral training or working experience in the area of biomedical research or related disciplines; (ii) a strong interest in cancer research; (iii) a good track record of research and publication in peer-reviewed scientific journals; (iv) a record of award of competitive research grants; and (v) a strong motivation for a future independent career. The appointee is expected to (a) develop significant independent research projects; (b) participate in applications for external competitive research grant; (c) supervise postgraduate research students; and (d) perform other duties as assigned. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Applicants should submit an online application and attach (1) a curriculum vitae with publication list; (2) a research plan; (3) a statement of teaching philosophy/experience; and (4) the names and contact information of three referees. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/med/acp . For enquiries, please contact Professor Gary TSE, Chairperson of the Department (e-mail: garytse@cuhk.edu.hk ). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001HM": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (250001HM)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (250001HM) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (250001HM) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 250001HM ) Description Department/Unit: Chow Yuk Ho Technology Centre for Innovative Medicine Closing Date: Until the post is filled. Chow Yuk Ho Technology Centre for Innovative Medicine (TCIM) is seeking a highly motivated early-career researcher with outstanding potential in regenerative medicine, biomaterials, or nanomedicine for the post of Research Assistant Professor. The applicant should have (i) a PhD degree in Polymer Materials Science, Nanomaterials Science, Biomedical Engineering, or a related discipline; (ii) first-author publications in high-impact journals; (iii) a strong theoretical foundation and independent research capabilities; (iv) demonstrate innovation and commitment to cutting-edge research; (v) a high integrity, responsibility, diligence, and excellent teamwork and communication skills; and (vi) a proficiency in written and spoken English. The appointee will work in the following research areas: 1.      Fundamental and applied studies on mesenchymal stem cells (MSCs) and induced pluripotent stem cells (iPSCs); 2.      Development of novel biomaterials and nanomedicines for regenerative medicine and disease therapy; and 3.      Design and application of engineered exosome-based drug delivery systems. The appointee will be expected to (a) develop and participate in independent/collaborative research projects; (b) seek external research grants; (c) supervise research assistants and students; (d) assist in laboratory management; and (e) perform other duties as assigned. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Applicants should submit the online application and attach (1) a curriculum vitae with a publications list; (2) a cover letter outlining motivation, research interests, key achievements, and peer recognition; and (3) full-text copies of 2-3 representative publications.  Review of applications continue until the position is filled. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Chow Yuk Ho Technology Centre for Innovative Medicine Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250001HW": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250001HW)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250001HW) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250001HW) Job Description Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors - ( 250001HW ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Mathematics and The Institute of Mathematical Sciences Closing Date: Until the posts are filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. The Department of Mathematics in CUHK has developed a strong reputation in teaching and research. Many of the faculty members are internationally renowned and are recipients of prestigious awards and honours. The graduates are successful in both academia and industry. The Department is highly ranked internationally, e.g., it is 66th, 63rd and 42nd in the 2023, 2024 and 2025 QS World University Rankings, and 42nd, 56th and 51st in the 2023, 2024 and 2025 US News Rankings, respectively. The Department is now inviting applications for substantiable-track faculty posts at all the academic levels. The appointees will be affiliated to both the Department and The Institute of Mathematical Sciences. Applicants should have (i) a relevant PhD degree in mathematics or related disciplines; (ii) an established track record in research, including publications; and (iii) a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Applicants should submit online application form, copies of qualification documents, a publication list and/or selected abstracts, a research plan, a teaching statement, together with the names and e-mail addresses of three to five referees (at least two on research and one on teaching) to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing January or September 2026, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to substantiation or longer-term appointment later. Review of applications will begin on September 1, 2025. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Mathematics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500012D": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Educational Leadership and Administration) (2500012D)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Educational Leadership and Administration) (2500012D) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Educational Leadership and Administration) (2500012D) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Educational Leadership and Administration) - ( 2500012D ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Educational Administration and Policy Closing date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Educational Administration and Policy is looking for distinguished scholars for appointment at various professoriate levels in the areas of Educational Leadership and Administration. The Department is one of the four Academic departments under the Faculty of Education of CUHK ( http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/ ), an international center for professional training and research in Education. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/eap . Applicants should have (i) excellent academic qualifications including a doctoral degree in educational administration, leadership or related discipline; (ii) a strong research background in areas that will contribute or add to the existing strengths of the Department; (iii) a track record of programmatic research and publications; and (iv) strong commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship. For Professor/ Associate Professor rank, applicants should have achieved a high standing in the relevant research field and demonstrated academic and international professional leadership. The appointee(s) will (a) play a key role in teaching and research initiatives in educational administration and leadership; (b) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (c) supervise postgraduate students; (d) obtain external competitive grants; and (e) assist in administrative matters. Concurrent leadership appointment in a research centre of the Faculty on educational leadership could also be considered for candidates with proven academic leadership and an outstanding track record in obtaining and managing diverse funded projects. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to funding and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Applicants may consider their applications unsuccessful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months after application. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Educational Administration and Policy Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500012E": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Foundation in Education and Policy Studies in Education) (2500012E)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Foundation in Education and Policy Studies in Education) (2500012E) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Foundation in Education and Policy Studies in Education) (2500012E) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (Foundation in Education and Policy Studies in Education) - ( 2500012E ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Educational Administration and Policy Closing date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Educational Administration and Policy is looking for distinguished scholars for appointment at various professoriate levels in the areas of Foundation in Education and Policy Studies in Education. The Department is one of the four academic departments under the Faculty of Education of CUHK ( http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/ ), an international center for professional training and research in Education. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.fed.cuhk.edu.hk/eap . Applicants should have (i) excellent academic qualifications including a doctoral degree in policy studies, early childhood education, ethics for teaching profession, sociology of education, philosophy of education, artificial intelligence in education or related discipline ; (ii) a strong research background in areas that will contribute or add to the existing strengths of the Department; (iii) a track record of programmatic research and publications; (iv) potential to obtain competitive research grants; and (v) strong commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship. For Professor/ Associate Professor rank, applicants should have achieved a high standing in the relevant research field and demonstrated academic and international professional leadership. The appointee(s) will (a) play a key role in teaching and research initiatives in foundation in education and policy studies in education; (b) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (c) supervise postgraduate students; (d) obtain external competitive grants; and (e) assist in administrative matters. Applicants should complete the online application form and upload a full curriculum vitae with details of three referees. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to funding and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Applicants may consider their applications unsuccessful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months after application. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Educational Administration and Policy Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500012N": {
      "title": "Job Description - Clinical Professor (Teaching) / Associate Clinical Professor (Teaching) (2500012N)",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professor (Teaching) / Associate Clinical Professor (Teaching) (2500012N) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professor (Teaching) / Associate Clinical Professor (Teaching) (2500012N) Job Description Clinical Professor (Teaching) / Associate Clinical Professor (Teaching) - ( 2500012N ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Closing Date: Until the position is filled Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for full or limited registration with the Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) training in histopathology (Anatomical Pathology); (iii) a higher qualification [MRCPath, FRCPA, FRCP(C), Diploma of American Board of Pathology (AP), or FHKAM(Pathology)]; (iv) subspecialty experience in Anatomical Pathology; (v) teaching experience in Anatomical Pathology; and (vi) track record of research and publication in Anatomical Pathology and teaching. The appointee will (a) undertake teaching and clinical duties; (b) supervise and coordinate course development for medical education; (c) provide guidance and consultation to trainees in the Department; (d) engage in research activities; and (e) plan and organize professional educational activities. Appointment will normally be made on fixed-term contract basis initially for up to three years, which may be extended or renewed subject to performance and mutual agreement, with the possibility of conversion to continuous appointment terms. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/med/acp . For enquiries, please contact Professor Gary TSE, Chairman of the Department (e-mail: garytse@cuhk.edu.hk ). The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anatomical and Cellular Pathology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000QR": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250000QR)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250000QR) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors (250000QR) Job Description Professors/ Associate Professors/ Assistant Professors - ( 250000QR ) Description Department/ Unit: Zhizhen School of Interdisciplinary Mathematical Sciences Closing date: Until the posts are filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. CUHK has established the Zhizhen School of Interdisciplinary Mathematical Sciences (\"Zhizhen School\" or \"the School\"). It aims to cultivate mathematical science talent in Hong Kong, aligning with the national aspiration to building China into a leading country in education, as well as the 14th Five-Year Plan’s vision of strengthening basic research. This also aligns with the aspiration in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region government’s policy address to develop Hong Kong as an international hub for post-secondary education and establish the “Study in Hong Kong” brand. Professor Shing-tung Yau is the Founding Director of Zhizhen School. The School will offer an eight-year training programme similar to that of Qiuzhen College in Tsinghua University which includes three years of mathematical foundation training, two years of scientific research training and three years of doctoral training. Students who fulfil the general academic and whole-person education graduation requirements will be awarded CUHK Bachelor and PhD degrees. The School will build a team of world-class scholars, who will participate in high-level scientific research, lead various academic activities of the School, and also be responsible for teaching and supervising students and postdoctoral fellows. The School is now inviting applications for substantiable-track faculty posts at all the academic levels. Applicants should have (i) a relevant PhD degree in mathematics or related disciplines; (ii) an established track record in research, including publications; and (iii) a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2025, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to substantiation or longer-term appointment later. Applicants please upload a full resume and attach copies of academic credentials, together with names and e-mail addresses of three to five referees (at least two on research and one on teaching) to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references. Review of applications will begin on May 15, 2025, and will continue until the positions are filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Zhizhen School of Interdisciplinary Mathematical Sciences Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000NC": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professors (250000NC)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professors (250000NC) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professors (250000NC) Job Description Research Assistant Professors - ( 250000NC ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Mathematics Closing Date: Until the posts are filled Founded in 1963, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is a forward-looking comprehensive research university with a global vision and a mission to combine tradition with modernity, and to bring together China and the West. The Department of Mathematics in CUHK has developed a strong reputation in teaching and research. Many of the faculty members are internationally renowned and are recipients of prestigious awards and honours. The graduates are successful in both academia and industry. The Department is highly ranked internationally, e.g., it is 41st, 66th and 63rd in the 2022, 2023 and 2024 QS World University Rankings, and 51st, 42nd and 56th in the 2022, 2023 and 2024 US News Rankings, respectively. The Department invites applications for multiple non-substantive-track positions at the Research Assistant Professor (RAP) level in Mathematical Artificial Intelligence . We seek exceptional researchers who combine deep engineering expertise with a passion for engineering-driven AI innovation. Applicants should have (i) a PhD in Management Science and Engineering, Computer Science , or a related discipline, with a focus on AI/ML theory, algorithms, or applications; (ii) a proven engineering expertise : hands-on experience transforming the theory into scalable production systems, backed by patented innovations; (iii) a proven research record in mathematical AI (e.g., optimization, dynamical systems, graph theory, probabilistic modeling) or adjacent fields with engineering impact; and (iv) fluency in prototyping and software development (e.g., Python, C++, CUDA, or ML frameworks) and interest in open-source collaboration. The positions provide opportunities to collaborate with faculty on cutting-edge projects at the math-AI interface and lead engineering-intensive research initiatives, and access to high-performance computing resources and industry partnerships. We encourage applicants who thrive at the intersection of theory and implementation, with a vision to bridge mathematical rigor with real-world AI challenges. Appointments will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years commencing August 2025, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Applicants should submit online application form, copies of qualification documents, a publication list and/or selected abstracts, together with the names and e-mail addresses of at least three referees to whom the applicant's consent has been given for their providing reference. Review of applications will begin on May 1, 2025 and will continue until the positions are filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Mathematics Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000L7": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (250000L7)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (250000L7) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (250000L7) Job Description Teaching Assistant(s) - ( 250000L7 ) Description Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology is recruiting full-time Teaching Assistant(s) in the following areas: 1. Business Economics 2. Operations Management Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor’s Degree, preferably a Higher Degree in Economics, Business, Operations Management, Supply Chain/ Logistics or a related discipline; (ii) a good command of spoken English & Chinese; (iii) good presentation skills; (iv) a meticulous attitude, a strong sense of responsibility as well as good interpersonal and management skills; and (v) willingness to work under pressure. Work outside normal office hours (including evenings, weekends) may be required.  Applicants who are near completion of the Master’s Degree will also be considered. The appointees will assist in lectures, tutorials, preparation of course materials, grading, student consultation or supervision, and other academic activities as assigned. Appointments will initially be made on a contract basis for one year commencing August 2025, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Decisions, Operations and Technology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=200000QG": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (200000QG)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (200000QG) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (200000QG) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) - ( 200000QG ) Description Department/Unit: School of Biomedical Sciences Closing Date: Until the posts are filled The School of Biomedical Sciences, Faculty of Medicine (CU Medicine) has three major thematic research programmes focusing on: cancer biology and experimental therapeutics; developmental and regenerative biology; and neural, vascular, and metabolic biology.  Further information is available at https://www3.sbs.cuhk.edu.hk/en/ thematic-research-programs . The School welcomes individuals who are highly devoted to innovative biomedical research and who value the opportunity to work in close collaboration with basic and clinical scientists to apply for the post(s) of full-time non-clinical Professor(s), Associate Professor(s), and Assistant Professor(s). Applicants should have (i) a PhD, MD, or DVM degree or its equivalent in the biological and biomedical sciences or related disciplines; (ii) experience in using cutting-edge technologies such as bioinformatics, single-cell spatial multi-omics, proteomics, metabolomics,  advanced microscopy and molecular imaging, gene editing, organoid, multi-electrode array,  transgenic animal and micromanipulation, in their studies; (iii) a competitive track record of research and publication in top peer-reviewed scientific journals in one or more related areas; and (iv) a good track record of external funding support.  Individuals with track record in research on cardiovascular function, neural development and neurodegenerative diseases, tumor microenvironment, cancer epigenetics and immunotherapy, senescence and aging, 3D genome, AI-driven drug discovery, systematic biology, and translational medicine with clinical relevance are particularly welcome. The appointee(s) is/are expected to lead a vigorous independent research programme aside from teaching undergraduate, postgraduate, medical and general education courses.  Our School is well-equipped with state-of-the-art technological platforms and further information is available at https://www3.sbs.cuhk.edu.hk/en/core-laboratories .  Appointee(s) will be provided with appropriate laboratory and office space and a start-up package commensurate with his/her qualification and experience. Appointment(s) will normally be made on a contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance, funding and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or tenured position later. For enquiries, please contact: sbs.med@cuhk.edu.hk Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Biomedical Sciences Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000JG": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (250000JG)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (250000JG) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (250000JG) Job Description Research Assistant Professor - ( 250000JG ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Information Engineering Closing date: Until the post is filled The Department of Information Engineering at The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) seeks outstanding candidates for Research Assistant Professorship (RAP) in the areas of AI for Health and Medicine with a focus on clinical applications, Embedded AI algorithms and systems, Autonomous Driving and Robotics systems. Applicants should have (i) a PhD in Computer Science or related field; (ii) demonstrated research ability in systems and AI, with focus on at least one of the applications in health, medicine, autonomous driving, and robotics. The successful candidate is expected to (a) conduct research in AI and systems; (b) pursue external research funding as Principal Investigator and Co-Investigator; (c) co-supervise undergraduate and graduate students; (d) teach relevant courses at undergraduate and graduate levels; and (e) contribute to service duties at department, faculty, and university levels.  The appointee will work closely with Prof. Guoliang Xing's research group in the department, focusing on advancing the field of embedded AI systems. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years.  Applicants should submit an online application and attach a full resume, a list of publications, a cover letter, together with names and e-mail addresses of three referees to whom the applicants' consent has been given for their providing references.  The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  Only shortlisted applicants will be notified. Further information about the Department is available at http://www.ie.cuhk.edu.hk/ . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Information Engineering Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000JB": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor (Clinical) (250000JB)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor (Clinical) (250000JB) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor (Clinical) (250000JB) Job Description Professor (Clinical) - ( 250000JB ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Otorhinolaryngology, Head and Neck Surgery Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Department is looking for a high-calibre professional for the post of Professor (Clinical) in Otorhinolaryngology, Head and Neck Surgery. Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) a solid relevant post-registration experience; (iii) full training and a higher qualification in otorhinolaryngology, head and neck surgery; (iv) expertise in a relevant subspecialty in otorhinolaryngology or head and neck surgery; (v) experience in and commitment to undergraduate and postgraduate clinical teaching; (vi) good track record of research funding and productivity as evidenced by high-impact peer-reviewed publications; (vii) outstanding academic administration skills and leadership in research development; and (viii) evidence of collaborative interactions. The appointee will (a) undertake clinical professional teaching for the undergraduate curriculum and postgraduate professional training; (b) conduct clinical research and collaborative research projects; (c) provide clinical service; (d) mentor junior doctors and researchers; and (e) assume major academic and administrative leadership roles. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for two years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the following: (i) full resume; (ii) copies of academic credentials; and (iii) full publication list. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Otorhinolaryngology, Head and Neck Surgery Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000I0": {
      "title": "Job Description - Part-time Lecturer(s) (250000I0)",
      "description": "Job Description - Part-time Lecturer(s) (250000I0) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Lecturer(s) (250000I0) Job Description Part-time Lecturer(s) - ( 250000I0 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Marketing Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled The Department of Marketing under the CUHK Business School now invites applications for the position of Part-time Lecturer(s) in the 2025 -26 academic year.  The appointee(s) should be able to teach Marketing courses at the undergraduate level such as Marketing Management and Marketing Research, and commit to daytime teaching on weekdays (Monday to Friday). Candidates should possess a higher degree in Marketing, Business, or a relevant discipline from a recognized university. Relevant tertiary-level teaching experience will be desirable. Appointment will be made on contract basis for four to five months commencing in August 2025 for Term 1 or December 202 5 for Term 2 , renewable subject to mutual agreement and good performance. Appointee(s) demonstrating outstanding performance may be considered favorably in case of full-time teaching vacancies. Review of candidates will be conducted on a rolling basis until the position(s) is/ are filled. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Marketing Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=250000GT": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (250000GT)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (250000GT) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) (250000GT) Job Description Professor(s)/ Associate Professor(s)/ Assistant Professor(s) - ( 250000GT ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Sports Science and Physical Education Closing Date: Until the position(s) is/ are filled This position requires a commitment to scholarly productivity, teaching excellence, and professional service. The successful candidate will be positioned to bridge many of the research sub-disciplines in the Department. Applicants should have (i) a PhD degree in sports/exercise science, kinesiology, public health or a closely related discipline ; (ii) e vidence of a strong record of publications in high-quality international journals, preferably in the areas of sports pedagogy and physical education, wearable technology and AI, exercise and rehabilitation science, or physical activity epidemiology and bioinformatics (iii) competence and experience in course teaching and research student supervision; and (iv) experience in programme administration and/or development. The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (b) supervise graduate students; (c) publish in top-tier journals related to sports and health; and (d) involve in the development and delivery of teaching programmes. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. For candidates with outstanding research/ scholarship credentials and very good teaching/ service records, substantiation may be considered at initial appointment. Salary will be highly competitive, and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Further information about the Department is available at https://www.spe.cuhk.edu.hk/eng/index.asp . Applicants should submit an online application and attach (1) a curriculum vitae with publication list; (2) a research plan; (3) a statement of teaching philosophy/experience; and (4) the names and contact information of three referees. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Sports Science and Physical Education Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500009K": {
      "title": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer(s)/Lecturer(s)/Assistant Lecturer(s) (2500009K)",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Lecturer(s)/Lecturer(s)/Assistant Lecturer(s) (2500009K) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Lecturer(s)/Lecturer(s)/Assistant Lecturer(s) (2500009K) Job Description Senior Lecturer(s)/Lecturer(s)/Assistant Lecturer(s) - ( 2500009K ) Description Department of Social Work Senior Lecturer(s) / Lecturer(s) / Assistant Lecturer(s) (Ref. 2500009K) Closing Date: Until the post(s) is / are filled. The Department of Social Work at CUHK is hiring Senior Lecturer(s)/Lecturer(s)/Assistant Lecturer(s). Applicants should (i) have a higher degree (for Senior Lecturer and Lecturer: a doctoral degree; for Assistant Lecturer: a Master’s degree) in social work or a related discipline; (ii) have at least eight years post-doctoral degree (for Senior Lecturer)/ four years post-master’s degree (for Lecturer) of teaching/professional experience and a proven record of teaching excellence (for Senior Lecturer); (iii) be registered social workers; (iv) have at least five years’ post-social work degree experience in social work practice in one or more of the following areas: human behavior and the social environment; family services; family counselling; family intervention; social policy; social welfare administration; micro social work service; medical social work; mental health; and rehabilitation; (v) demonstrate ability for high quality teaching of undergraduate and/or postgraduate courses; and (vi) show firm commitment to social work education as well as excellence in teaching and scholarship. The appointees will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses during daytime and evening; (b) supervise and coordinate students’ fieldwork in social service agencies; (c) assist in curriculum development; and (d) contribute their practical experience to teaching and curriculum design. Appointments will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years commencing August 2025, renewable subject to good performance and mutual agreement. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Social Work Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500004G": {
      "title": "Job Description - Lecturer(s) (2500004G)",
      "description": "Job Description - Lecturer(s) (2500004G) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Lecturer(s) (2500004G) Job Description Lecturer(s) - ( 2500004G ) Description Department / Unit: The Nethersole School of Nursing Closing Date: Until the positions are filled Applicants should (i) have a relevant doctoral degree/terminal degree with teaching/professional experience; or a Master's degree in Nursing plus four years’ post-qualification clinical nursing experience; (ii) be licensed to practise with The Nursing Council of Hong Kong; and preferably (iii) have recent clinical practice or teaching experience (particularly in general medical-surgical, orthopaedic, or obstetric nursing). The appointee(s) will (a) teach nursing students at the University and in clinical settings, with some shift work; (b) coordinate courses; and (c) perform other duties as assigned by the Director or his delegates. Appointment(s) will initially be made on contract basis for two years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings: (i) full curriculum vitae; (ii) copies of academic credentials and professional qualification certificate(s) (e.g. Diploma/ Certificate in Education); (iii) evidence of teaching performance and course evaluation, if any; and (iv) other relevant documents to support the application. Further information about the School is available at https://www.nur.cuhk.edu.hk . The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : The Nethersole School of Nursing Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2500000E": {
      "title": "Job Description - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (2500000E)",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (2500000E) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (2500000E) Job Description Associate Professor / Assistant Professor - ( 2500000E ) Description Department of Psychology Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (Ref. 2500000E) Closing Date: Until the post is filled The Department is keen to enhance its reputation as a world-class research hub and generator of knowledge that prides itself over teaching and mentorship. It hopes that a new faculty member in the field of Clinical Psychology will embrace that agenda with the support of abundant facilities at the Department. Applicants should have (i) a PhD or equivalent in clinical psychology which is registrable for the professional practice of clinical psychology in Hong Kong; (ii) demonstrated potential/ ability to build a strong publication track record and obtain grants; (iii) international experience; and (iv) strong commitment to supervise students. Scholars with demonstrated academic leadership, research excellence, a track record of obtaining external competitive funding and rich experience in students’ supervision are particularly encouraged to apply. The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (b) supervise students’ projects and theses; (c) undertake research; and (d) assist in administrative duties. Appointment will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2025, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Salary and fringe benefits will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The University offers a comprehensive fringe benefit package, including medical care, a contract-completion gratuity for an appointment of two years or longer, and housing benefits for eligible appointee. Applications will be accepted until the post is filled. Further information about the Department and its programmes is available at http://www.psy.cuhk.edu.hk. For enquiries, please contact the Department via e-mail at infopsy@cuhk.edu.hk. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Psychology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2400035D": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (2400035D) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (2400035D) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant - ( 2400035D ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Closing Date: Until the post is filled Applicant should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) a specialist qualification in obstetrics and gynaecology; (iii) experience in teaching medical students; and (iv) a track record of research. The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (b) provide clinical service; and (c) assist in clinical research. Appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2400031I": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant(s) (2400031I) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant(s) (2400031I) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant(s) - ( 2400031I ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Closing Date: Until the position(s) are filled The Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK), is an academic department based at the Prince of Wales Hospital (PWH), a 1,637-bed tertiary referral teaching hospital. The hospital provides a wide range of acute specialist services, including stroke, obstetric, cardiac and trauma centres. The clinical service provides anaesthesia for 14,000 operations in the main operating theatres, with one third being emergency cases, with an additional 2000 anaesthetics are administered in other areas. The 26-bed adult intensive care unit provides medical and surgical critical care for approximately 1800 patients per year. The department is committed to achieving excellence in education and research and maintains active educational and research collaborations with numerous international and mainland institutions. Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with the Hong Kong Medical Council); (ii) a higher qualification in anaesthesia or intensive care registrable with the Hong Kong Medical Council Specialist Registry ; (iii) a minimum of five years' relevant post registration experience; and (iv) teaching/training experience in relevant disciplines. The appointee(s) will perform clinical duties in either Prince of Wales Hospital (PWH) or CUHK Medical Centre (CUMC), assist in the teaching of undergraduate and postgraduate students, support training of junior doctors, assist in clinical research and other duties as assigned by the Department Chairperson. Salary will follow the standard pay scale of the Clinical Academic track of the Chinese University of Hong Kong and will depend on successful applicant’s prior experience and pay grade at their current or recent appointments. Appointment(s) will initially be made on contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above via the CUHK career site. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240002T4": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (240002T4)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant (240002T4) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant (240002T4) Job Description Teaching Assistant - ( 240002T4 ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Marketing Closing Date: Until the position is filled The applicants should: (a)  Possess a relevant university degree in majors such as Marketing, Business, Psychology, Economics, and Statistics. Other majors will be considered as well; (b)  Have strong people skills and excellent command of written and spoken English, as well as spoken Chinese (Cantonese and/or Mandarin); (c)  Demonstrate proactive work attitude, a strong sense of responsibility, great attention to detail, and genuine motivation to learn; (d)  Be capable of assisting in tutorials, laboratory/ practical classes, compilation of course materials, and other academic activities under guidance; and (e)  Be proficient in Microsoft Office (e.g. Word, Excel and PowerPoint). Skills in programming and using statistical software (such as SPSS, R or Python) and survey software (such as Qualtrics) will be advantages . Relevant office experience, including internship experience, will also be a bonus . Please upload a cover letter in addition to curriculum vitae explaining why you are interested in this position. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years commencing as soon as possible, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Marketing Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240002VS": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (240002VS) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant (240002VS) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant - ( 240002VS ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Closing Date: Until the post is filled Applicant should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) a specialist qualification in Reproductive Medicine; (iii) experience in teaching medical students; and (iv) a track record of research. The appointee will (a) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; (b) provide clinical service; and (c) assist in clinical research. Appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk . Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240002SJ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor (240002SJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor (240002SJ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor (240002SJ) Job Description Professor - ( 240002SJ ) Description Department of Social Work Professor (Ref. 240002SJ) Closing date: Until the post is filled As a world-leading centre of social work education and research, the Department is dedicated to developing and disseminating scientific rigorous and socially impactful social work knowledge for human betterment and social development, such as in the niche areas on aging, mental health, family, and social policy. We aspire, through our research and evaluation work, to improve the lives of vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, deepen our understanding of social issues and promote evidence-based practice locally and globally. The Department is looking for candidates who embrace these goals and values. The Department is seeking a well-established scholar who will contribute to the continuous development and enhancement of the Department in social work research and education. More specifically, our ideal candidate is expected to: Have a clear vision of and be dedicated to quality social work research, education and professional training ; Have a strong record of scientific research and publications in social work or social administration; Be experienced in capacity building in an academic department of social work; Be committed to nurturing and mentoring future thought leaders in the department, discipline and profession; Possess transformational leadership and excellent communication skills; Be enthusiastic and experienced in fostering transdisciplinary, cross-disciplinary, and international collaborations; and Understand Hong Kong, China, and Asian culture and initiate dialogues among different cultures The Department and the University are committed to attracting top talent and offer competitive salary and benefit packages commensurate with qualifications and experience. Outstanding candidates may be specially considered for substantive appointment forthwith. Application Procedure The University only accepts and considers applications submitted online for the post above. For more information and to apply online, please visit http://career.cuhk.edu.hk. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Social Work Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240002E8": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant  (240002E8) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Professional Consultant  (240002E8) Job Description Clinical Professional Consultant - ( 240002E8 ) Description Department/Unit: Faculty of Medicine Closing Date: Until the post is filled Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with the Hong Kong Medical Council); (ii) a higher qualification in a medical specialty acceptable to the Faculty; (iii) experience in teaching medical students (honorary or adjunct teacher in a medical school is also acceptable); and (iv) developed local leadership and portfolio in one or two of the following areas: clinical skills teaching, simulation, workplace assessment, medical assessments, bioethics, professionalism, communication skills, e-learning or any other areas of medical education. The appointee will teach medical students at the Prince of Wales Hospital (PWH) or associated teaching units. He/she should be dedicated to the development of medical education in addition to fulfilling some clinical duties as a clinician at PWH or associated teaching units. Appointment will initially be made on a contract basis for up to three years, renewable subject to mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Faculty of Medicine Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240001OZ": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Lecturer(s) / Lecturer(s) (Full-time / Part-time) (240001OZ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Lecturer(s) / Lecturer(s) (Full-time / Part-time) (240001OZ) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Lecturer(s) / Lecturer(s) (Full-time / Part-time) (240001OZ) Job Description Assistant Lecturer(s) / Lecturer(s) (Full-time / Part-time) - ( 240001OZ ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Chinese Medicine Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/are filled Applicants should have (i) a Master's degree in Chinese Medicine or related disciplines; (ii) the certificate of registration of Chinese medicine practitioner recognized by the Chinese Medicine Council of Hong Kong; (iii) at least 4 years’ Chinese medicine clinical experience (including acupuncture); and (iv) clinical teaching experience at university level. The appointee(s) will (a) undertake teaching duties; (b) provide clinical service; (c) participate in the development of Chinese medicine; and (d) carry out research tasks. The appointee(s) will work at the clinics managed under the School of Chinese Medicine.  Appointment(s) will initially be made on a 1-year contract, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Chinese Medicine Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240001HB": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor (Landscape Architecture)  (240001HB)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor (Landscape Architecture)  (240001HB) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor / Associate Professor (Landscape Architecture)  (240001HB) Job Description Professor / Associate Professor (Landscape Architecture) - ( 240001HB ) Description School of Architecture Professor / Associate Professor (Landscape Architecture) (Ref. 240001HB) Closing Date: Until the post is filled. The Chinese University of Hong Kong is one of the world’s leading universities. Its location makes it one of the most exciting places to research and teach architecture. The School of Architecture has a world-class, research-led, and professionally connected learning environment. It embraces new approaches to architectural education and cross-disciplinary research that impact on society and the profession. The School of Architecture at the Chinese University of Hong Kong is seeking an outstanding candidate to provide academic leadership for its new Master of Landscape Architecture (MLA) Programme. Applicants should possess (i) a PhD degree in Landscape Architecture, Planning, Architecture, Environmental Studies or a related discipline. Applicants with international recognition in the field will be highly appreciated. Preference will be given to candidates with an active research agenda and/or design practice that addresses pressing environmental, ecological and urban challenges in the Asian region. We are particularly interested in candidates who can contribute to the development of interdisciplinary research and teaching that connect landscape architecture with allied built environment disciplines, including, but not limited to, Architecture, Urban Design and Planning. Appointments will normally made on a contract basis for up to three years initially commencing August 2025, which, subject to performance, funding availability and mutual agreement, may lead to a longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Outstanding candidates may be considered for substantive appointment upon initial appointment. To apply for the post, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, CV, portfolio, teaching statement, research statement, together with names/ e-mail addresses of three referees with consent for providing references. Appointment level and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s qualifications and experience. The CUHK School of Architecture is actively building a more diverse and inclusive environment. Qualified individuals from underrepresented sections of society are encouraged to apply. Enquiries may be directed to Ms. Sylvia Kwok, School Manager at arc.appointment@cuhk.edu.hk Review of applications and shortlisting will start in July / August 2024 until the post is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Architecture Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240001P1": {
      "title": "Job Description",
      "description": "Job Description - Professional Consultant(s) (Full-time / Fractional-time) (240001P1) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professional Consultant(s) (Full-time / Fractional-time) (240001P1) Job Description Professional Consultant(s) (Full-time / Fractional-time) - ( 240001P1 ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Chinese Medicine Closing Date: Until the post(s) is/are filled Applicants should have (i) a Bachelor’s degree in Chinese Medicine or related disciplines; (ii) the certificate of registration of Chinese medicine practitioner recognized by the Chinese Medicine Council of Hong Kong; (iii) at least 10 years’ Chinese medicine clinical experience (including acupuncture); and (iv) clinical teaching experience at university level. The appointee(s) will (a) provide clinical service; (b) undertake clinical teaching; (c) participate in the development of Chinese medicine; and (d) carry out research tasks.  The appointee(s) will work at the clinics managed under the School of Chinese Medicine.  Appointment will initially be made on a 1-year contract, renewable subject to performance and mutual agreement. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Chinese Medicine Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240001GL": {
      "title": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (240001GL)",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (240001GL) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (240001GL) Job Description Professor(s) / Associate Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) - ( 240001GL ) Description Department/ Unit: CUHK Interdisciplinary Artificial Intelligence Research Institute Closing Date: Until the post(s) is / are filled CUHK Interdisciplinary Artificial Intelligence Research Institute (IAIRI) is set up jointly by The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) and Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory in 2021, with the aim to encourage and promote interdisciplinary research utilizing AI technology. The Institute is supported by Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Science and Faculty of Medicine. We are now seeking dedicated and creative scholars to help build up our newly established Institute through active research and strong commitment to teaching and mentoring of students. The Institute invites applications from outstanding academics in emerging fields with potential for scientific and scholarly breakthroughs above and beyond our existing recruitment to join CUHK at the level of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor. Multiple positions in the general area of artificial intelligence and its applications, including machine learning, computer vision, natural language processing, and AI applications in various domains are available. Outstanding candidates from diverse disciplines in computing, distributed systems, statistics, optimization, applied mathematics, medicine and other related areas are also welcome. Successful candidates will be jointly appointed by the Institute and the Faculties to best align with the candidate's work. This is a broad search open to all areas of data science including but not limited to databases and systems, fundamental machine learning, interface between optimization and machine learning, natural language processing, visions and robotics, Bayesian learning, causal inference, and decision making under uncertainty. Research collaborations across borders are highly encouraged and abundant research resources will be matched to facilitate the related research. Appointment(s) will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Applicants are encouraged to apply by June 30, 2025 to ensure earlier consideration, but the search will continue until positions are filled. To apply online, please complete the on-line application form together with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, research statement, teaching statement, 2 or 3 most significant research publications, and contact information for at least three referees. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : The Chinese University of Hong Kong Interdisciplinary Artificial Intelligence Research Institute Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=240000KD": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant / Associate Professor in Digital Technology and Computational Design (240000KD)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant / Associate Professor in Digital Technology and Computational Design (240000KD) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant / Associate Professor in Digital Technology and Computational Design (240000KD) Job Description Assistant / Associate Professor in Digital Technology and Computational Design - ( 240000KD ) Description School of Architecture Assistant / Associate Professor ( Digital Technology and Computational Design ) (Ref. 240000KD) Closing Date: Until the post is filled. The Chinese University of Hong Kong is one of the world’s leading universities. Its location makes it one of the most exciting places to research and teach architecture. The School of Architecture has a world-class, research-led, and professionally connected learning environment. It embraces new approaches to architectural education and cross-disciplinary research that impact on society and the profession. The School of Architecture is seeking an outstanding candidate to make significant contributions to research and teaching of Digital Technology and Computational Design, expanding ongoing explorations in design for robotic construction and innovation in the construction industry. The appointees will advance an individual research agenda focused on academic contributions and experimental applications, building research collaborations within the University and beyond. Applicants should (i) have a PhD degree in a subject area relevant to architecture, digital design or other related areas OR (ii) a professional Master’s degree in architecture and not less than 4 years (with professional registration) or 6 years (without professional registration) of practical experience in architecture thereafter. Applicants with international recognition in the field will be highly appreciated. Preference will be given to candidates with an excellent record of studio teaching and research. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to performance, funding availability and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Outstanding candidates may be considered for substantive appointment upon initial appointment. To apply for the posts, please complete the online application form, and submit a letter of interest, CV, portfolio, together with names/e-mail addresses of three referees with consent for providing references. Appointment level and salary will be commensurate with the applicant’s qualifications and experience. The CUHK School of Architecture is actively building a more diverse and inclusive environment. Qualified individuals from underrepresented sections of society are encouraged to apply. To explore the School and the posts further, please visit our website at https://www.arch.cuhk.edu.hk/people/careers . Enquiries may be directed to Ms. Sylvia Kwok, School Manager at arc.appointment@cuhk.edu.hk . Review of applications and shortlisting will start in June / July 2024 until the position is filled. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Architecture Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=2300034O": {
      "title": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (2300034O)",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (2300034O) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant(s) (2300034O) Job Description Teaching Assistant(s) - ( 2300034O ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Finance Closing date: Until the positions are filled The Department of Finance is now seeking Teaching Assistants for its MSc Programme in Finance. Applicants should have a good Bachelor's Degree, preferably a Master's Degree in Finance, Economics or related fields.  In addition, applicants should have (i) good command of spoken English & Chinese (ii) good presentation skills, (iii) a meticulous attitude, a strong sense of responsibility as well as good interpersonal and management skills; and (v) willingness to work under pressure. The appointee will assist in lectures, tutorials, preparation of course materials, grading, student consultation or supervision, and other academic activities as assigned. Appointment will initially be made on contract basis for two years, renewable subject to mutual agreement and good performance.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Finance Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=230001B4": {
      "title": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (non-clinical)  (230001B4)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (non-clinical)  (230001B4) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (non-clinical)  (230001B4) Job Description Research Assistant Professor(s) / Assistant Professor(s) (non-clinical) - ( 230001B4 ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Psychiatry Closing Date: Until the posts are filled The Department of Psychiatry at the Faculty of Medicine, The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) is recruiting Research Assistant Professor(s )/ Assistant Professor(s) (non-clinical) within the following research areas:- Neuroscience Sleep and circadian Digital mental health This is an exciting opportunity for outstanding young investigators to play a leading role in advancing mental health research programmes related to the above-mentioned research areas at CUHK. The successful candidates are expected to (i) hold a PhD degree in a relevant field with post-doctoral experience; and (ii) have ample experiences in the field of any of the above-mentioned research areas and mental health, as evidenced by publications in international journals. They must have passion to advance by establishing a dynamic, creative and internationally oriented research group and attract external research funding. Appointment of Research Assistant Professor(s) will initially be made on contract basis for up to two years commencing as soon as possible, renewable subject to good performance, funding availability and mutual agreement. Appointment of Assistant Professor(s) (non-clinical) will normally be made on contract basis for up to two years initially, which, subject to good performance, funding availability and mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation. Applicants should complete the on-line application form and upload the followings: • A full curriculum vitae; • Copies of academic credentials; • A full list of the applicant's scientific publications indicating the five most important publications; • Copies of all publications on which the applicant wishes to be evaluated; • A brief survey of the applicant's most important research results and research plans for the next three years, including research management and research grants; and • An outline of how the applicant’s future research strategy would build on current research, identifying how it would complement existing research in the above-mentioned research areas and mental health research programmes of CUHK. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Psychiatry Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=220002Z2": {
      "title": "Job Description - Director, School of Hotel & Tourism Management, CUHK Business School (220002Z2)",
      "description": "Job Description - Director, School of Hotel & Tourism Management, CUHK Business School (220002Z2) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director, School of Hotel & Tourism Management, CUHK Business School (220002Z2) Job Description Director, School of Hotel & Tourism Management, CUHK Business School - ( 220002Z2 ) Description Department/ Unit: School of Hotel and Tourism Management Closing date: Until the position is filled About CUHK Business School (Faculty of Business Administration) The CUHK Business School is a pioneer in business education in Hong Kong. Since its establishment in Hong Kong in 1963, the CUHK Business School has gained world recognition of nurturing business leaders with immense contributions in Asia Pacific region. The Business School comprises two schools – Accountancy and Hotel & Tourism Management; and four departments – Finance, Decision Sciences & Managerial Economics, Management, and Marketing. The Business School has been offering a comprehensive range of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes (DBA, MBA, MSc, MAcc, EMBA, MPhil, PhD) with over 4,600 students, as well as executive education. It has one of the most extensive alumni networks in the region, with over 40,000 alumni around the world. About the School of Hotel & Tourism Management The School of Hotel & Tourism Management (SHTM) is an integral part of the CUHK Business School. It was established in 1998 in view of the growing significance of the hospitality industry in Hong Kong and Asia. The SHTM’s mission is to develop leaders for the hospitality and real estate industries through a broad-based business education. It now comprises a dynamic group of academic and professional teaching staff members supported by a team of teaching, research and administrative support staff as well as a food and beverage team. The SHTM offers programmes at different levels to nurture future leaders for the hospitality and real estate industries.  The following is a list of the undergraduate and postgraduate programmes: BBA in Hospitality and Real Estate MSc in Real Estate MPhil-PhD in Business Administration The CUHK Business School now seeks to appoint a Director of School of Hotel & Tourism Management.  Reporting to the Dean of Business Administration, the Director will serve as a key member of the Business School’s leadership team and will have overall responsibility for academic leadership and administration in the SHTM.  The ideal candidate should be a visionary and collaborative leader who excels at enhancing the quality and reputation of SHTM’s academic programmes and research, and strengthening connection with business communities, and should have: a strong track record of scholarly eminence in the area of hospitality and/or real estate and demonstrate commitment to research and teaching excellence; a doctoral degree in hospitality, real estate or other related business disciplines; strong record of teaching and research experiences in a research university or other tertiary institutions; administrative experiences in previous tertiary institutions and/or companies with strong communication and networking skills; an international outlook as well as regional knowledge; and strong established networks in hospitality and real estate industries. Previous studying/working experiences outside Hong Kong are highly valued. Appointment of Directorship will be made on fixed terms basis for three years and subject to renewal, as appropriate. An academic appointment will also be made either on substantive rank (with tenure) or fixed terms concurrently. Application Procedure The CUHK Business School is engaging the executive search firm, Perrett Laver Ltd., on this search. Applications should consist of a full CV detailing academic and professional qualifications and relevant achievements. It should be accompanied by a cover letter describing how candidates meet the selection criteria, why the appointment is of interest, what they believe they can bring to the role, and a statement describing strengths and experiences in advancing the research, teaching, connection with the profession as well as community engagement in their previous and/or current institutions. For a confidential discussion about the position, please contact Mr Kenny Mak via  Kenny.Mak@perrettlaver.com or +852 3702 6493. Review of applications will begin in December 2022, and will continue until the position is filled.  Shortlisted candidates may be invited for informal discussions, on campus visits and interviews subsequently, as appropriate. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : School of Hotel and Tourism Management Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=220000DH": {
      "title": "Job Description - Clinical Lecturer(s) (220000DH)",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Lecturer(s) (220000DH) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Lecturer(s) (220000DH) Job Description Clinical Lecturer(s) - ( 220000DH ) Description Department/ Unit: Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Closing Date: Until the posts are filled The Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care is based at the Prince of Wales Hospital (PWH), a 1,637 bed tertiary referral teaching hospital managed by the Hospital Authority (HA) and affiliated with The Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK). The hospital provides a wide range of acute specialist services, including both a cardiac and trauma centre. Each year we deliver anaesthetic services for 14,000 operations in the main operating theatre, with one third being emergency cases. An additional 2000 anaesthetics are administered in the labour ward and other areas outside the operating theatre suite. The Intensive Care Unit provides adult medical and surgical critical care for approximately 1700 patients per year. Applicants should have (i) a medical qualification (approved for registration with The Medical Council of Hong Kong); (ii) experience/strong interest in anaesthesia and/or intensive care; and (iii) preferably some teaching experience.  A good command of spoken and written English is required (proficiency in Cantonese will be an advantage but not essential). Duties include (a) providing high quality clinical services in anaesthesia and intensive care; (b) teaching undergraduate and postgraduate courses; and (c) other duties as assigned by the Department Chairman. Appointment will be made on contract basis for one year, renewable subject to mutual agreement and satisfactory performance. Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    },
    "https://cuhk.taleo.net/careersection/cu_career_teach/jobdetail.ftl?job=210000LA": {
      "title": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (210000LA)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor (210000LA) Go to the main content section. Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor (210000LA) Job Description Assistant Professor - ( 210000LA ) Description Department/Unit: Department of Social Work Closing Date: Until the post is filled As a world-leading centre of social work education and research, the Department is dedicated to developing and disseminating scientific, rigorous and socially impactful social work knowledge for human betterment and social development. We aspire, through our research and evaluation work, to improve the lives of vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, deepen our understanding of social issues and promote evidence-based practice locally and globally. The Department is looking for candidates who embrace these goals and values. Scholars specializing in any of the following research areas are welcome to apply for the post: - clinical social work - children and family - gerontology - macro social work theories and practice Applicants should (i) have a relevant PhD degree; (ii) have a strong publication track record and proven ability to obtain grants; and (iii) demonstrate potential in conducting research to generate academic and social impact. Being registered social workers and having professional expertise or substantial work experience in clinical or macro social work practice will be advantageous. The appointee will (i) undertake research and (ii) teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses. Appointments will normally be made on contract basis for up to three years initially, which, subject to mutual agreement, may lead to longer-term appointment or substantiation later. Applications are open until the post is filled. [Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref. 200000G9) are under consideration and need not re-apply in this instance.] Job : Professoriate, Teaching and Research Academic Posts Organization : Department of Social Work Unposting Date : Ongoing"
    }
  },
